Rio","lane":"Virtuoso/Fora","mor":"consortia","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Santa Teresa Hotel RJ (MGallery)","lane":"consortia","mor":"consortia","tier":"premier","note":"verify MGallery vs Relais & Châteaux affiliation"},{"name":"Janeiro Hotel, Leblon","lane":"Fora/consortia","mor":"consortia","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Private Carnival + Búzios villas","lane":"DMC AOR","mor":"DMC","tier":"ultra"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-22.9068,"lng":-43.1729}}'::jsonb, 90),
  ('rio-lagartos-mexico', '10S', 'Río Lagartos', 'Mexico', 'Spring breeding grounds of the flamingos **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"expedition","tropical"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Ría Lagartos Biosphere Reserve — Yucatán''s flamingo capital; ~35 km boat safari, 400+ bird species","Flamingos breed Apr-Jul, counts near 40,000 — opposite of Celestún''s Nov-Mar peak","Las Coloradas pink lagoons colored by halophilic bacteria/algae; Mexico''s #2 salt operation; no-swim default, drones banned","Remote coast — nearest full trauma care Mérida ~2-2.5 hr; Tizimín ~1 hr, Valladolid ~1.5 hr","Cash economy (one ATM, runs dry); certified federal guides; sunscreen banned on-boat"],"safety":{"emergency_number":"911","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"nearest_trauma":"Mérida private hospitals (~2-2.5 hr); Valladolid hospital (~1.5 hr) w/ 24-hr ambulance transfer; Tizimín (~1 hr) basic","remote_flag":true,"activity_fires":["boat-safari life vests + CONANP-licensed operator","sun/dehydration open water","no-touch/no-flush wildlife","Las Coloradas no-swim salt lagoon","remote medevac distance","mangrove/mosquito"]},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"2026-03-15","peak":"Apr-Jul (flamingo breeding, ~40,000 birds)","fire_date":"2026-03-01","shoulder":"Aug-Oct (green/rainy)","booking_lead_weeks":"4-8","notes":"Río Lagartos flamingos peak Apr-Sep (breeding) — OPPOSITE window to Celestún (Nov-Mar). Follow-the-sun within Yucatán. Las Coloradas pinkest Mar + Jul-Aug. Sharpen on live tracking."},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Flamingo boat safari (Ría Lagartos)","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC (Amstar) / GetYourGuide-Viator affiliate","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/rio-lagartos-l146496/ttd/","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC (Amstar) / GetYourGuide-Viator affiliate"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Las Coloradas pink lakes (no swim)","tier":"essential","commission_path":"activity affiliate + non-commissionable entry pass-through","source":"https://travelbooksfood.com/las-coloradas-pink-lakes-of-mexico-yucatan","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"activity affiliate + non-commissionable entry pass-through"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Crocodile night tour","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC / cooperative referral","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g1168987-d1965637-Reviews-Rio_Lagartos_Adventures-Rio_Lagartos_Yucatan_Peninsula.html","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"DMC / cooperative referral"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Mayan mud bath (Baño Maya)","tier":"essential","commission_path":"bundled in boat tour","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g1168987-d1965637-Reviews-Rio_Lagartos_Adventures-Rio_Lagartos_Yucatan_Peninsula.html","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"bundled in boat tour"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"San Felipe fishing village","tier":"essential","commission_path":"content halo → dining/lodging affiliate","source":"https://www.letstraveltomexico.com/rio-lagartos-yucatan/","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"content halo → dining/lodging affiliate"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"El Cuyo kite / quiet beach","tier":"essential","commission_path":"kite-school + guesthouse affiliate/bedbank","source":"https://www.letstraveltomexico.com/el-cuyo-yucatan/","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"kite-school + guesthouse affiliate/bedbank"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to see flamingos at Río Lagartos?","a":"April through July, the breeding concentration, when counts reach near 40,000 birds — the exact opposite window from Celestún, which peaks November–March. Counts swing year to year with water level and salinity, so book the reserve and the season, not a promised number, and sharpen on live tracking before committing to a date.","source":"letstraveltomexico.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can you swim in the Las Coloradas pink lakes?","a":"Default no — plan for it. Las Coloradas is a working industrial hypersaline salt operation (Mexico''s #2), not a swim beach; entry is rule-bound and guide-mandatory, and drones are banned by the salt company. A 2026 report suggests a limited, pre-booked 10-minute swim window may again be permitted at specific spots, but treat that as unconfirmed and volatile and default to the no-swim expectation.","source":"travelbooksfood.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What else will I see besides flamingos?","a":"A full biosphere: 400+ logged bird species, crocodiles on the after-dark night run (mellow and family-friendly for older kids), the white halophilic-clay \"Baño Maya\" mud bath, and the salt-flat geology behind the pink. The reserve is a dedicated birding vertical once the Wildlife SI opens.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"Is there a beach at Río Lagartos?","a":"Yes — three quiet ones. Cancunito is a white-sand swim beach near town, San Felipe (12 km west) is a pastel fishing village with fresh seafood, and El Cuyo (45 min east) is a resort-free barrier-beach village inside the biosphere with steady side-shore wind for kitesurfing, peaking Dec–Feb.","source":"letstraveltomexico.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is Río Lagartos safe right now?","a":"Yes — freely bookable. Río Lagartos is in Yucatán, one of only two Mexican states rated US State Dept Level 1 \"Exercise Normal Precautions.\" It is a calm working fishing village; the bigger planning items are the remoteness and the cash economy — one ATM in town that is known to run dry, so arrive with pesos.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Río Lagartos?","a":"Distance to trauma care, not crime. The town has only a basic clinic; Tizimín is ~1 hr, Valladolid''s hospital ~1.5 hr (with 24-hr ambulance transfer for serious cases), and Mérida''s full private hospitals ~2–2.5 hr. Serious injury means a long road transfer, so build the medevac distance into expectations, especially for older travelers, and carry insurance.","source":"yucatanmagazine.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the flamingo boat safari safe?","a":"Yes, with a licensed operator. Confirm life vests aboard and book a CONANP-licensed / federally certified cooperative rather than a freelance boatman at the dock; the top real risk on the 2.5–4 hr open-water run is sun and dehydration — and note sunscreen is banned on-boat to protect the ecosystem, so rely on hat, clothing and shade.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Río Lagartos & Las Coloradas: Flamingos and Pink Lakes | TravelWell.World","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["flamencos Río Lagartos","Las Coloradas Yucatán","reserva de la biosfera Ría Lagartos","tour flamencos Yucatán","baño Maya Río Lagartos","El Cuyo kitesurf"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","tropical"],"ultra":[{"name":"Chablé Yucatán","type":"Mérida luxury hacienda base (hub-and-spoke)","distance":"~25 min from Mérida; day-trip flamingos","earning_lane":"Fora advisor lane","tier":"ULTRA","note":"No branded ultra on the flamingo coast; luxury = hacienda base + private CONANP charter"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Río Lagartos, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":21.5983,"lng":-88.1592}}'::jsonb, 91)
insert into public.destinations (id, region_code, name, country, line, status, depth, img, sub_region, si, feel, tier_range, price_band, draw_rank, data, position) values
  ('roatan-honduras', '10S', 'Roatán, Honduras (Bay Islands)', 'Honduras', 'Roatán', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Honduras', '{"diveglobal","tropical"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Roatán sits on the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef, the second-largest coral-reef system on earth; Bay Islands ranked highest in coral health in the 2015 Mesoamerican assessment.","30+ dive shops on the west side; ~30 named dive sites within a 10-minute boat ride off West Bay/West End, with walls dropping past 100 ft and the El Aguila/Odyssey wrecks.","The Roatán Aggressor IV liveaboard runs Sat->Sat (18 guests, ~24-27 dives) across Roatán, Cayos Cochinos, and Utila.","Whale sharks are snorkel-only and protected; Utila (a short hop from Roatán) offers year-round potential peaking late March-April.","Roatán has an on-island recompression chamber (Cornerstone Hyperbaric, adjacent to Anthony''s Key Resort; DAN IPPN partner) — a first-response advantage for wall diving."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hyperbaric_chamber":"Cornerstone Hyperbaric Chamber & Clinic, Sandy Bay (adjacent to Anthony''s Key Resort) — on-island recompression chamber + ER/lab/pharmacy, DAN International Preferred Provider Network partner","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Honduras (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance, pulled live), plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"air_access_verified":"Direct air into Juan Manuel Gálvez Intl (RTB), Roatán — Bay Islands reachable without transiting mainland gang zones","no_fly_after_diving":"18-24 hours before RTB departure flight (DAN protocol)","environmental":["west-wall depth discipline","currents on walls/channels","dengue (CDC)","bottled water only"]},"timing":{"peak_season":"mid-December to April (dry season); whale-shark peak late March-April; secondary Oct-Dec","best_visibility":"July-September","curve_start":"late November (dry-season); early March (whale-shark spike)","inflection":"December peak; late-March-April whale-shark peak","fire_date":"early-to-mid November (dry-season peak); mid-February (whale-shark spike)","booking_lead_months":"4-6","off_season_fill":"September-November (rain / hurricane-fringe) — value window, visibility-driven dive messaging","dive_calendar":true},"jewels":[{"name":"West End Wall + Mary''s Place","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"premier","commission_path":"dive-resort package (Fora) / own-CLIA liveaboard","source":"https://sundiversroatan.com/roatan-diving/","hook":"West End Wall is a top-tier wall dive","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"West End Wall is a top-tier wall dive","commission":"dive-resort package (Fora) / own-CLIA liveaboard"},{"name":"Shark Dive — Cara a Cara (via Waihuka)","si_tag":"Diving/GEA","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"excursion via DMC/dive-resort (Fora)","source":"https://roatan.online/cara-cara-shark-dive","hook":"face-to-face with 8–15 Caribbean reef sharks at ~70 ft; ~$120 pp + 15% tax","si":"Diving/GEA","blurb":"face-to-face with 8–15 Caribbean reef sharks at ~70 ft; ~$120 pp + 15% tax","commission":"excursion via DMC/dive-resort (Fora)"},{"name":"Cayos Cochinos","si_tag":"Diving/Liveaboard","tier":"premier","commission_path":"own-CLIA liveaboard","source":"https://divemagazine.com/scuba-diving-travel/americas-caribbean/aggressor-adventures-roatan-aggressor-liveaboard-highlights","hook":"protected archipelago of pristine, less-dived reefs — a Roatán Aggressor itinerary highlight","si":"Diving/Liveaboard","blurb":"protected archipelago of pristine, less-dived reefs — a Roatán Aggressor itinerary highlight","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard"},{"name":"El Aguila & Odyssey wrecks","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"premier","commission_path":"dive-resort package (Fora)","source":"https://diveintolife.blog/scuba-diving-in-roatan-honduras-west-bay-west-end/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"dive-resort package (Fora)"},{"name":"Whale-shark snorkel (Utila day-trip)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"day-trip excursion via DMC (Fora)","source":"https://www.thisisutila.com/post/utila-s-whale-shark-season-when-to-come-and-what-to-expect","si":"expedition","commission":"day-trip excursion via DMC (Fora)"},{"name":"Dolphin Encounter (Anthony''s Key Resort)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"AKR package/excursion (Fora)","source":"https://anthonyskey.com/dolphin-programs/","hook":"get-in-the-water dolphin program in a natural lagoon; a 50-year AKR institution","si":"expedition","blurb":"get-in-the-water dolphin program in a natural lagoon; a 50-year AKR institution","commission":"AKR package/excursion (Fora)"},{"name":"Gumbalimba Park (ziplines, capuchins, iguanas, macaws)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC excursion (Fora/affiliate)","source":"https://roatan.online/gumbalimba-park","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC excursion (Fora/affiliate)"},{"name":"Iguana Farm (near French Cay, 2,700+ iguanas)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC excursion (affiliate)","source":"https://roatantourbase.com/excursion-guides/our-favorite-things-to-do-and-see-in-coxen-hole","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC excursion (affiliate)"},{"name":"Punta Gorda — Garífuna culture (UNESCO)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"cultural excursion via DMC (Fora/affiliate)","source":"https://roatantourbase.com/excursion-guides/our-favorite-things-to-do-and-see-in-coxen-hole","hook":"Roatán''s oldest settlement; UNESCO-recognized Garífuna heritage, with the April 12 anniversary celebration","si":"expedition","blurb":"Roatán''s oldest settlement; UNESCO-recognized Garífuna heritage, with the April 12 anniversary celebration","commission":"cultural excursion via DMC (Fora/affiliate)"},{"name":"West Bay Beach","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","commission_path":"anchors West Bay resort/villa stays (Fora / MoR villa)","source":"https://www.royalcaribbean.com/inspire/what-is-roatan-known-for","hook":"Roatán''s iconic white-sand shoreline; warm shallows, reef snorkeling straight off the sand","si":"Tropical/Beaches","blurb":"Roatán''s iconic white-sand shoreline; warm shallows, reef snorkeling straight off the sand","commission":"anchors West Bay resort/villa stays (Fora / MoR villa)","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Roatán safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes, with the mandatory logged disclosure — the danger the advisory names sits on the mainland, not on the island. Honduras is US State Department Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" (reissued December 10, 2024, for crime), but State''s own text carves out the Bay Islands (Roatán, Utila, Guanaja) as areas with \"a concentration of resources\" that \"are better policed,\" and Roatán is reached by direct air into RTB without transiting the mainland gang corridors.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2024-12-10","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The load-bearing risk is mainland crime, and the plan is to stay in-zone. Violent crime and gang activity concentrate in the San Pedro Sula, Tegucigalpa, and Comayagua corridors, and Gracias a Dios Department carries a Level 4 \"Do Not Travel\" rating — all on the mainland. Fly direct into RTB, keep the trip airport → island, and never route overland through the gang zones.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2024-12-10","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is diving Roatán''s walls dangerous — and can I fly out afterward?","a":"Wall diving rewards depth discipline and respect for the no-fly window, and Roatán has an unusual first-response advantage. Recreational divers work the crest and upper wall (≤60–100 ft); wreck and deep-wall profiles trend technical and are certification-gated. Allow no-fly-after-diving of 18–24 hours before your RTB flight, and note the on-island Cornerstone Hyperbaric Chamber (adjacent to Anthony''s Key Resort, a DAN partner) — a genuine safety edge for a wall-diving island. **What makes Roatán''s diving special? ** *(Dive Liveaboards / Diving)* Roatán delivers a serious wall reef within minutes of the dock plus a rare repeat-rate track record. Within a 10-minute boat ride off West Bay/West End you reach ~30 named dive sites, from a 15-ft sandy playground with feeding eagle rays to 100-ft+ wall drop-offs, wrecks, and canyon swim-throughs; CoCo View Resort claims the highest repeat rate of any dive resort worldwide (1,600+ guests five times over).","source":"anthonyskey.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How much is the Roatán reef fee, and is it required?","a":"Yes, it is mandatory and it is small. The Roatán Marine Park conservation fee is $10/year or $5/day, non-commissionable, and it funds the very reef you came to dive and snorkel — present it as the reef''s cover charge, never buried.","source":"roatan.online, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is Roatán good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — Roatán runs a genuine adults-only luxury lane on top of the diving. Ibagari Boutique Hotel is adults-only (12+), holds a Michelin Key 2025, and sits between West Bay and West End; private West Bay villas and sunset-cocktail liveaboard finales round out the romance product.","source":"guide.michelin.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can I snorkel with whale sharks from Roatán?","a":"Yes, via a day-trip to neighboring Utila, and only by snorkel. Utila is one of the few places on earth with year-round whale-shark potential, peaking late March–April; the animals are protected, so it is surface snorkeling only — no diving with them and no touching.","source":"thisisutila.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"adventure"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Roatán, Honduras (Bay Islands) — Diving, Liveaboards & West Bay Beach | TravelWell.World","search_language":"es-HN","local_keywords":["buceo Roatán","West Bay Roatán","Islas de la Bahía","tiburón ballena Utila","arrecife mesoamericano buceo","hoteles de buceo Roatán","cámara hiperbárica Roatán"],"long_tail_en":["Roatán diving guide","Roatán liveaboard Aggressor","West Bay Beach Roatán","whale shark snorkel Utila from Roatán","is Roatán safe to visit 2026","Roatán hyperbaric chamber"],"hreflang":["en","es-HN"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Roatán"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"diveglobal","status":"live"},{"si":"tropical","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Ibagari Boutique Hotel","lane":"Fora / Virtuoso preferred","mor":"Fora","tier":"Ultra/Luxury","note":"adults-only, Michelin Key 2025, boutique dive center"},{"name":"Las Verandas Hotel & Villas (Pristine Bay)","lane":"Fora / Virtuoso","mor":"Fora","tier":"Luxury","note":"villa resort + Black Pearl golf"},{"name":"Turquoise Bay Dive & Beach Resort","lane":"Fora","mor":"Fora","tier":"premier","note":"remote NE all-inclusive dive"},{"name":"Private West Bay villas (Arca / Lighthouse Estates)","lane":"MoR villa rung","mor":"MoR","tier":"Luxury","note":"full-villa buyout + DMC concierge"},{"name":"Roatán Aggressor private charter","lane":"own-CLIA","mor":"CLIA","tier":"Ultra/Premium","note":"full 18-berth whole-boat buyout"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Roatán, Honduras (Bay Islands), Honduras"},"geo":{"lat":16.3,"lng":-86.53}}'::jsonb, 92),
  ('ruta-de-las-flores-el-salvador', '10S', 'Ruta de las Flores, El Salvador', 'El Salvador', 'Ruta de las Flores', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'El Salvador', '{"culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L1","advisory_reissued":"2026-06-25","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L1)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"San Salvador (SAL / Comalapa) + ~1.5–2 hr drive west; no visa for US stays under 90 days","volcano":{"name":"Santa Ana / Volcán Ilamatepec","status":"active, monitored","elevation_m":2381,"last_eruption":2005,"access":"guided summit only; scheduled departures; subject to activity-alert closure"},"health_notes":["bottled/purified water","dengue present — repellent, esp. green season"],"trauma_note":"Santa Ana / San Salvador hospitals; complex cases → US medical evacuation"},"timing":{"peak":"Dry season Nov–Apr (wildflower carpet Nov–Feb; year-round Juayúa weekend food festival); coffee-blossom micro-peak ~May","inflection":"Late Oct as rains taper; mid-to-late Apr before coffee blossom","green_season":"May–Oct (warm/wet, lush, lowest rates)","fire_date":"Mid-to-late October (dry-season crest, curve-start Nov 1 minus 1–2 wks); mid-April for the May coffee-blossom micro-peak"},"jewels":[{"name":"Juayúa Feria Gastronómica (weekend food festival)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC/Viator/GetYourGuide weekend-anchor package; festival free, transport/guide/lodging earns","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC/Viator/GetYourGuide weekend-anchor package; festival free, transport/guide/lodging earns","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Coffee-finca tour + cupping (Apaneca / Ataco)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC add-on or Santa Leticia direct-stay bundle; operator/hotel commissionable","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC add-on or Santa Leticia direct-stay bundle; operator/hotel commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Santa Ana volcano turquoise crater + Cerro Verde","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Guided-summit product via DMC/Viator; guiding/transport commissionable, park fees not","source":"https://sallysees.com/santa-ana-volcano-hike/ | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The signature GEA hero shot — a radioactive-bright sulphur lake in an active crater","si":"expedition","blurb":"The signature GEA hero shot — a radioactive-bright sulphur lake in an active crater","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Guided-summit product via DMC/Viator; guiding/transport commissionable, park fees not","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Lake Coatepeque (volcanic caldera lake)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"Lakeside boutique-hotel bookings (Cardedeu/Equinoccio) + boat excursions via operator","source":"https://www.booking.com/city/sv/coatepeque.html | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Lakeside boutique-hotel bookings (Cardedeu/Equinoccio) + boat excursions via operator","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Apaneca Laguna Verde + Enganches/Ausol canopy zipline","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC/operator activity affiliate","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Crater lake ~5 km from Apaneca plus Central America''s longest cloud-forest ziplines","si":"expedition","blurb":"Crater lake ~5 km from Apaneca plus Central America''s longest cloud-forest ziplines","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC/operator activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Los Chorros de la Calera / Siete Cascadas waterfall hike (Juayúa)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Local guide via DMC; commissionable through operator (guided-only)","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Terraced falls with cliff jumps and rappels. The 7 Waterfalls hike requires a mandatory guide — flash-flood, slick-rock, and cliff-jump hazards make guided mandatory","si":"expedition","blurb":"Terraced falls with cliff jumps and rappels. The 7 Waterfalls hike requires a mandatory guide — flash-flood, slick-rock, and cliff-jump hazards make guided mandatory","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Local guide via DMC; commissionable through operator (guided-only)","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Concepción de Ataco street art + coffee","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Mural-walk + coffee-finca combo via DMC; workshop fees via operator","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"El Salvador''s most photogenic mural town — indigenous-history murals, Mirador de la Cruz, indigo-dye workshops, weekend street festival","si":"culture","blurb":"El Salvador''s most photogenic mural town — indigenous-history murals, Mirador de la Cruz, indigo-dye workshops, weekend street festival","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Mural-walk + coffee-finca combo via DMC; workshop fees via operator","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Nahuizalco Mercado Nocturno (night market)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Evening add-on to route itinerary; craft purchases direct","source":"https://www.visitelsalvador.ai/blog/ruta-de-las-flores-guide-complet-villages | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"One of the few places you''ll see women in traditional Pipil dress; wicker-craft workshops and a rare evening artisan market","si":"culture","blurb":"One of the few places you''ll see women in traditional Pipil dress; wicker-craft workshops and a rare evening artisan market","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Evening add-on to route itinerary; craft purchases direct","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Joya de Cerén — Pompeii of the Americas (UNESCO)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Guided heritage day trip via DMC/Viator; site entry non-commissionable","source":"https://www.viator.com/San-Salvador-attractions/Joya-de-Ceren-Archaeological-Site/d5585-a15755 | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A 7th-century Maya farming village buried and preserved by volcanic ash; El Salvador''s only UNESCO World Heritage site. Open 9–4, closed Mondays; on-site museum","si":"culture","blurb":"A 7th-century Maya farming village buried and preserved by volcanic ash; El Salvador''s only UNESCO World Heritage site. Open 9–4, closed Mondays; on-site museum","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"Guided heritage day trip via DMC/Viator; site entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Tazumal ruins (Chalchuapa)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Combined Maya-heritage day trip w/ Joya de Cerén via DMC/operator; entry non-commissionable","source":"https://andysworldjourneys.com/2025/10/16/joya-de-ceren-and-tazumal-ancient-history-in-el-salvador/ | Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"El Salvador''s most important pyramids/ceremonial platforms, ~40 min from Joya de Cerén — the two pair into one Maya-heritage day","si":"culture","blurb":"El Salvador''s most important pyramids/ceremonial platforms, ~40 min from Joya de Cerén — the two pair into one Maya-heritage day","when":"year-round","commission":"Combined Maya-heritage day trip w/ Joya de Cerén via DMC/operator; entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is El Salvador safe to travel in 2026?","a":"Yes — El Salvador is at US Level 1, \"Exercise Normal Precautions,\" reissued June 25, 2026, the lowest advisory tier and the same level as much of Western Europe. Gang activity has declined significantly since 2022, driving violent-crime rates down and holding the country at that tier; aggregator sites still show stale \"Level 2\" text, so the official page and live site win — re-verify before booking.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is the Juayúa food festival?","a":"The Feria Gastronómica is the route''s flagship weekend market: every Saturday and Sunday, 11am–5pm, free entry, cash only, with the plaza filling with grills and pots — grilled meats $6–9, seafood ~$7, soups $3–4, pupusas ~$0.60, and roughly $10–20 feeds one person across multiple dishes. *[Culinary]*","source":"visitelsalvador.ai, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Is Joya de Cerén worth visiting?","a":"Yes — it is El Salvador''s only UNESCO World Heritage site, a 7th-century Maya farming village buried and preserved by volcanic ash, earning the name \"Pompeii of the Americas.\" Open 9–4 and closed Mondays with an on-site museum, it pairs with the Tazumal ruins (~$5 entry, ~40 min away) into one Maya-heritage day. *[Culture & Heritage]*","source":"viator.com + andysworldjourneys.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is the Santa Ana volcano hike dangerous?","a":"It is managed, not casual. Santa Ana (Volcán Ilamatepec, 2,381 m) is an active, monitored volcano with a turquoise sulphur crater lake and volcanic gas near the rim; the ~4–5 hour summit hike is guided-only, at scheduled departure times, and is subject to closure on activity alerts. Do not attempt it unguided, and confirm open status before booking.","source":"sallysees.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What outdoor adventures are on the Ruta de las Flores?","a":"The GEA spine runs from Santa Ana''s turquoise crater and Cerro Verde to Lake Coatepeque (a volcanic caldera lake beneath the volcano), plus Apaneca''s cloud-forest canopy ziplines (Los Enganches ~420 m lines) and the Laguna Verde crater lake ~5 km from Apaneca. Waterfall hikes at Los Chorros / Siete Cascadas round it out. *[GEA]*","source":"visitelsalvador.ai + sallysees.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where do couples stay on the Ruta de las Flores?","a":"Two romance bookends: coffee-finca boutique on the route itself — Hotel Santa Leticia, a 19-room working-estate lodge from ~USD 78/night — or lakeside luxe on Lake Coatepeque, where Cardedeu Residence is a 5-star hotel and Equinoccio a boutique lakeside stay with balcony rooms over the water. There is no international five-star flag on the route. *[Romance]*","source":"lastfrontiers.com + booking.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Guided-only adventure and mountain roads. The Siete Cascadas 7-waterfall hike (~6 hrs) requires a mandatory guide (~$15/person) because of flash-flood, slick-rock, and cliff-jump hazards; canopy ziplines are operator-run with harness and briefing. The route itself is a cobblestone-and-switchback mountain drive — go in daylight, watch for highland fog, and prefer a local driver at night.","source":"visitelsalvador.ai, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Ruta de las Flores, El Salvador — Coffee Towns, Santa Ana Volcano & the Flower Route | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-SV","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","local_keywords":["Ruta de las Flores El Salvador","Volcán Santa Ana","Juayúa festival gastronómico","Concepción de Ataco murales","Laguna Verde Apaneca","tour de café Ruta de las Flores","Lago de Coatepeque hotel","Joya de Cerén Pompeya de América"],"hreflang":["en","es-SV"],"primary_keyword":"Ruta de las Flores"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"},{"si":"culinary","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"property":"Hotel & Restaurante Santa Leticia (Apaneca)","note":"Boutique coffee-finca ceiling on the route itself; 19 rooms, on-farm coffee program","earning":"hotel commission via consortia/bedbank","mor":"hotel/OTA","tier":"$$–$$$"},{"property":"Cardedeu (5-star) / Equinoccio + private villas, Lake Coatepeque","note":"Caldera-lake luxe bookend under Santa Ana","earning":"hotel commission (Cardedeu/Equinoccio); villas referral/affiliate only","mor":"hotel for flags; Airbnb/VRBO for villas","tier":"$$$–$$$$"},{"property":"San Salvador city 5-star bookend","note":"Arrival/departure luxe anchor; where international-flag commission lives (verify availability)","earning":"hotel commission via preferred/Virtuoso program","mor":"hotel","tier":"$$$–$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Ruta de las Flores, El Salvador, El Salvador"},"geo":{"lat":13.8722,"lng":-89.7928}}'::jsonb, 93),
  ('san-andres-colombia', '10S', 'San Andrés & Providencia, Colombia', 'Colombia', 'Coral islet, seven-colour sea **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Colombia''s Caribbean Coast', '{"tropical","liveaboard","romance","culture"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","premier","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["San Andrés — the ''Sea of Seven Colors'' — is Colombia''s Caribbean crown jewel, ringed by coral with 40+ mostly-shallow, high-visibility dive sites.","Providencia + Santa Catalina sit on the third-largest barrier reef in the world; Providencia rebuilt after Hurricane Iota (2020) and is open to tourism in 2026.","The Raizal are a Black Colombian Afro-Caribbean people; 20,000–30,000 speak San Andrés–Providencia Creole (Islander English) and most are trilingual.","Rondón — fish, conch, cassava, plantain and yam simmered in coconut milk — is the island''s signature dish (''run down'').","Mandatory Tourist Card (Tarjeta de Turismo) ~COP 153,000 (2026), bought at the airline counter before boarding the flight to ADZ."],"safety":{"emergency":"123","hospital":"Hospital Departamental Clarence Lynd Newball (San Andrés); hyperbaric/decompression chamber at Timothy Britton Hospital, San Andrés; serious cases referred off-island to mainland or US","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","risk_codes":["C","T","U","K","N"],"risk_code_meanings":{"C":"Crime — violent crime (murder, assault, robbery), drugging (scopolamine/burundanga), extortion, express kidnapping occur throughout Colombia incl. cities (island crime skews to petty/beach theft + motorcycle snatch-and-grab)","T":"Terrorism — attacks possible with little/no warning; car bombs, grenades, IEDs, drones (mainland-weighted)","U":"Unrest — demonstrations can shut roads and turn violent","K":"Kidnapping or Hostage-Taking — kidnapping-for-ransom reported (mainland-weighted)","N":"Natural Disaster — mainland volcano/earthquake/landslide; archipelago hurricane/tropical-storm exposure (Hurricane Iota, Nov 2020)"},"named_danger":["Arauca","Cauca excl Popayán","Valle del Cauca excl Cali","Norte de Santander","Venezuela border ~10km"],"archipelago_in_named_danger":false,"island_crime_note":"island petty-crime (beach theft, motorcycle snatch-and-grab, scooter accidents) is lower and different from mainland violent crime; country-level advisory still renders in full at consent","consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Colombia (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance, pulled live) + traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"air_access_verified":"ADZ (Gustavo Rojas Pinilla Intl) — direct international from Panama City (Copa, year-round) + domestic Colombian hubs; no nonstop US, but 1-stop via BOG/PTY (Avianca, Copa, LATAM). Providencia reached by ~20-min inter-island flight or catamaran.","remote_flag":true,"water":"bottled","vaccinations":"dengue/chikungunya/Zika present (peak rainy months); use insect protection; check CDC","scopolamine_caution":"''devil''s breath''/burundanga drugging — country-level; concentrates on mainland; never accept drinks/food from strangers"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec–Apr (dry); true peak January, then Feb–Mar (Colombians'' favorite domestic island)","inflection_curve_start":"early December","fire_date":"mid-to-late November (Dec–Jan peak); ~4–6 weeks before Semana Santa (late-Feb/early-Mar) for the Easter spike","event_peaks":[{"event":"Christmas–New Year","dates":"Dec 20–31","note":"maximum annual congestion; ADZ seats + rooms sell out"},{"event":"Semana Santa (Holy Week)","dates_2026":"Mar/Apr","note":"intense domestic coastal surge"}],"off_season_fill":"Sep–Nov (green season, lowest crowds, best deals); Jul–Aug secondary dry spell = best weather-to-cost; note higher dengue in rainy months"},"jewels":[{"name":"Sea of Seven Colors (Spratt Bight + lagoon)","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"hotel + boat-tour affiliate","source":"https://colombia.travel/en/san-andres-island","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the seven-shade turquoise-to-cobalt water off the North End and the Aquarium/Haynes Cay flats; the island''s signature image","si":"tropical","blurb":"the seven-shade turquoise-to-cobalt water off the North End and the Aquarium/Haynes Cay flats; the island''s signature image","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"hotel + boat-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Johnny Cay","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"GetYourGuide/Viator day-trip affiliate + park entry (non-comm)","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/colombia/san-andres-and-providencia/san-andres/attractions/johnny-cay-natural-regional-park/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"protected 4-ha coral islet ~1.5 km off San Andrés Town, coconut groves and the best white-sand beach around; colectivo boats from the town beach","si":"tropical","blurb":"protected 4-ha coral islet ~1.5 km off San Andrés Town, coconut groves and the best white-sand beach around; colectivo boats from the town beach","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"GetYourGuide/Viator day-trip affiliate + park entry (non-comm)"},{"name":"La Piscinita","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day-tour affiliate + on-site entry (non-comm)","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g3493965-d3228746-Reviews-La_Piscinita-San_Andres_San_Andres_Island_San_Andres_and_Providencia_Department.html","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"calm natural snorkel pool south of El Cove, dive board + water slide, reef fish, seafood restaurant + gear rental","si":"tropical","blurb":"calm natural snorkel pool south of El Cove, dive board + water slide, reef fish, seafood restaurant + gear rental","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"day-tour affiliate + on-site entry (non-comm)"},{"name":"West View (Mermaid Cave)","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day-tour affiliate + entry (non-comm)","source":"https://travelhapp.com/inspiration/things-to-do-in-san-andres-and-providencia","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"day-tour affiliate + entry (non-comm)"},{"name":"Rocky Cay + San Luis beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"San Luis hotel + day-tour affiliate","source":"https://colombia.travel/en/san-andres-island","hook":"walk-out cay off the quieter San Luis east coast, shallow wading to a wreck, the island''s mellow beach zone","si":"tropical","blurb":"walk-out cay off the quieter San Luis east coast, shallow wading to a wreck, the island''s mellow beach zone","commission":"San Luis hotel + day-tour affiliate"},{"name":"El Cove","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"island-tour affiliate","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/colombia/san-andres-and-providencia/san-andres/attractions/la-piscinita/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the island''s deepest natural anchorage on the West side, quiet local-life counterpoint to the North End","si":"tropical","blurb":"the island''s deepest natural anchorage on the West side, quiet local-life counterpoint to the North End","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"island-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Sea of Seven Colors reef dives + walls (Blue Wall, The Pyramid, Blue Diamond wreck)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards / Diving","tier":"essential","commission_path":"PADI operator direct/affiliate (Banda, Sharky)","source":"https://bandadive.com/en","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards / Diving","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"PADI operator direct/affiliate (Banda, Sharky)"},{"name":"Providencia barrier reef (third-largest on earth)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards / Diving","tier":"premier","commission_path":"Providencia dive operator direct + inter-island flight","source":"https://colombia.travel/en/providencia","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"wall and reef diving off Providencia/Santa Catalina, wilder and less-visited than San Andrés","si":"Dive Liveaboards / Diving","blurb":"wall and reef diving off Providencia/Santa Catalina, wilder and less-visited than San Andrés","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"Providencia dive operator direct + inter-island flight"},{"name":"Providencia + Crab Cay + McBean Lagoon","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","commission_path":"Providencia DMC/boutique + marine-park fee (non-comm)","source":"https://cuppatocopatravels.com/south-america/colombia/guide-isla-de-providencia-colombia/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the quiet-honeymoon jewel: Crab Cay ranked the island''s 1 snorkel spot, the McBean Lagoon marine park, near-empty coves","si":"romance","blurb":"the quiet-honeymoon jewel: Crab Cay ranked the island''s 1 snorkel spot, the McBean Lagoon marine park, near-empty coves","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"Providencia DMC/boutique + marine-park fee (non-comm)"},{"name":"San Luis sunset stays","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","commission_path":"San Luis hotel affiliate + host","source":"https://colombia.travel/en/san-andres-island/native-inns","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the mellow east-coast beach strip, sunset-side quiet, small hotels and native inns for a low-key honeymoon","si":"romance","blurb":"the mellow east-coast beach strip, sunset-side quiet, small hotels and native inns for a low-key honeymoon","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"San Luis hotel affiliate + host"},{"name":"Raizal culture + Islander Creole","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"cultural-tour affiliate + native-inn stay","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raizal","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a living Afro-Caribbean nation: Creole English, Baptist chapels, kinship ties across the western Caribbean","si":"culture","blurb":"a living Afro-Caribbean nation: Creole English, Baptist chapels, kinship ties across the western Caribbean","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"cultural-tour affiliate + native-inn stay"},{"name":"Rondón + coconut cuisine","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"food-tour affiliate + restaurant","source":"https://colombiaone.com/2025/09/02/colombia-food-san-andres/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the \"run down\" seafood-in-coconut-milk stew, breadfruit, crab, conch; a Raizal food-and-culture experience","si":"culture","blurb":"the \"run down\" seafood-in-coconut-milk stew, breadfruit, crab, conch; a Raizal food-and-culture experience","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"food-tour affiliate + restaurant"},{"name":"Morgan''s Cave","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"island-tour affiliate + entry (non-comm)","source":"https://colombiaone.com/2023/12/21/guide-visit-san-andres-island-colombia/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"legendary Henry Morgan pirate-treasure hideout, now a small theme park/museum with exhibits and dance shows","si":"culture","blurb":"legendary Henry Morgan pirate-treasure hideout, now a small theme park/museum with exhibits and dance shows","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"island-tour affiliate + entry (non-comm)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What are the best beaches and cays on San Andrés?","a":"Johnny Cay is the headline — a protected 4-ha coral islet ~1.5 km off San Andrés Town with the best white sand around, reached by colectivo boat — plus calm snorkel pools at La Piscinita and West View, and mellow Rocky Cay off San Luis. The lagoon is the famed \"Sea of Seven Colors.\"","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is San Andrés good for scuba diving?","a":"Yes — it''s a shallow-water reef diver''s dream, with 40+ dive sites mostly at ~10–12 m, high-visibility and beginner-friendly, run through island PADI centers like Banda and Sharky. Providencia adds wall diving on the third-largest barrier reef in the world. Note it''s day-boat reef diving, not liveaboard-berth product.","source":"divescover.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Is Providencia good for a quiet honeymoon?","a":"Yes — Providencia is the quiet-honeymoon jewel: near-empty coves, the McBean Lagoon marine park, and Crab Cay (its #1 snorkel spot, ~USD $6 park fee) reached by express boat. It''s rebuilt and open after Hurricane Iota (2020); reach it by ~20-minute inter-island flight or catamaran.","source":"cuppatocopatravels.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What language and culture will I find on San Andrés?","a":"A living Raizal Afro-Caribbean nation: 20,000–30,000 people speak San Andrés–Providencia Creole (Islander English) and most are trilingual, descended from 18th-century Jamaican settlers and enslaved Africans. The signature plate is rondón — fish, conch and root vegetables simmered in coconut milk.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is San Andrés safe to visit right now?","a":"Colombia is at US State Dept Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" (issued 2026-03-31, codes C·T·U·K·N), but the San Andrés/Providencia archipelago sits ~700 km offshore and is NOT in the named Level-4 Do-Not-Travel areas (all on the mainland). Island crime skews to petty/beach theft, not mainland violent crime — but the country advisory still renders in full at consent.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real day-to-day risk on the island?","a":"Not the mainland headlines — the island''s real risks are petty/beach theft, motorcycle snatch-and-grab, scooter accidents and sea/riptide hazards. Renting a scooter or golf cart is the classic island loop, and scooter crashes plus snatch-and-grab are the two most common tourist mishaps: helmet on, valuables off the seat, drive in daylight.","source":"travelsafe-abroad.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is diving here safe, and what about flying afterward?","a":"Yes, with standard scuba discipline — shallow, low-current, high-viz sites. The two fires: honor the 18–24 hr no-fly surface interval before an ADZ or inter-island flight (easy to violate on a short trip), and note the decompression chamber is at Timothy Britton Hospital on San Andrés — a boat or flight away from a Providencia dive.","source":"divingsquad.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Andrés & Providencia, Colombia — Sea of Seven Colors Diving, Beaches & Raizal Culture | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-CO","long_tail_en":["things to do in San Andres Colombia","San Andres diving Sea of Seven Colors","is San Andres safe 2026","Providencia island Colombia guide","San Andres tourist card cost 2026","Johnny Cay day trip San Andres","Providencia Crab Cay snorkeling"],"local_keywords":["San Andrés qué hacer","buceo San Andrés","Providencia","tarjeta de turismo San Andrés","Johnny Cay San Andrés","Cueva de Morgan","rondón San Andrés"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["tropical","Dive Liveaboards / Diving","romance","culture"],"ultra":[{"name":"Casa Harb","type":"design boutique — island top-end (luxury, NOT palace-ultra)","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred where participating + host","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Decameron cluster (Isleño/San Luis/Los Delfines/Aquarium)","type":"mass-market all-inclusive","routing":"Online-Agency (OA) lane + host","tier":"premium (mass AI)"},{"name":"GHL Sunrise Hotel (Sunrise Beach)","type":"mid-market beachfront workhorse, Spratt Bight","routing":"GDS/bedbank + host","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Casa Iguana del Mar (villa)","type":"award-winning design villa, reef + white sand","routing":"MoR villa + host","tier":"luxury (thin)"},{"name":"Deep Blue (Providencia)","type":"boutique standout, Crab Cay gateway","routing":"direct/host","tier":"premium (remote boutique)"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Andrés & Providencia, Colombia, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":12.5847,"lng":-81.7006}}'::jsonb, 94),
  ('san-blas-guna-yala-panama', '10S', 'San Blas / Guna Yala, Panama', 'Panama', 'Guna Yala, island by island **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Panama', '{"tropical","romance","expedition","culture"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_date":"2024-09-23 (reissued; verified live 2026-07-07)","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":"Charter flights Albrook (PAC) → El Porvenir (PVE) / Corazón de Jesús (CZJ), ~40–45 min, ~$400/pax; OR 4x4 (steep rain-sensitive Cartí road, ~4–5 hrs) + boat, through Guna Cartí checkpoint (passport + ~$20/pax foreigner entry fee, cash, no ATMs)","remote_flag":true,"medevac_note":"No hospital in Guna Yala; most cays have no clinic; serious cases require medevac to Panama City / US (can exceed $50,000) — comprehensive medevac insurance mandatory","health_note":"Year-round dengue/malaria/zika/chikungunya risk; malaria-risk area — consult travel clinic on prophylaxis; drink bottled/treated water","gate_result":"PASS — Guna Yala/San Blas verified NOT in any L4/L3 named area of the Sept 23, 2024 Panama advisory (Level 2 country-wide). Bin = freely bookable (L2). Verified live 2026-07-07."},"timing":{"peak":"dry season Dec–Apr (calmer seas for sailing + the Colombia crossing)","inflection":"Oct–Nov (winter-escape + honeymoon + dry-season sailing dates on sale)","fire_date":"mid-to-late September (curve-start − 1–2 weeks); charters sell out ahead","off_season":"May–Nov green/rainy — value + solitude window, weather-tolerant travelers"},"jewels":[{"name":"Cayos Holandeses (Dutch Cays) sandbar","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"multi-day charter / premium day-trip via DMC","source":"https://www.seasanblas.com/blog/cayos-holandeses-one-of-the-best-san-blas-islands-to-visit","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the remote outer cluster — is widely rated the best snorkeling in the San Blas archipelago","si":"Tropical/Beaches","blurb":"the remote outer cluster — is widely rated the best snorkeling in the San Blas archipelago","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"multi-day charter / premium day-trip via DMC"},{"name":"Natural Pool / Starfish spot (Piscina Natural)","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"essential","commission_path":"island-hopping day tour via DMC","source":"https://www.seasanblas.com/blog/complete-guide-to-visiting-san-blas-islands-panama","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical/Beaches","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"island-hopping day tour via DMC"},{"name":"Isla Pelícano / Cayos Limones lagoon","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day tour / short cabaña stay","source":"https://nomadsailors.com/blog/cayos-limones/","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical/Beaches","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"day tour / short cabaña stay"},{"name":"Castaway-island overnight cabaña","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC cabaña package or private charter overnight","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotels-g298434-San_Blas_Islands_Guna_Yala_Region-Hotels.html","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"DMC cabaña package or private charter overnight"},{"name":"Isla Perro (Dog Island) wreck snorkel","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day tour / charter stop","source":"https://sanblasadventures.com/san-blas-snorkeling/","si":"expedition","commission":"day tour / charter stop"},{"name":"Panama → Cartagena sailing charter (3–5 days)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"charter / CLIA lane — highest-value bookable in region","source":"https://sanblasadventures.com/boat-colombia-to-panama/general-information/","si":"expedition","commission":"charter / CLIA lane — highest-value bookable in region"},{"name":"Guna mola textiles + living culture (1925 revolution, matrilineal congress, Dulegaya)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage (future)","tier":"essential","commission_path":"cultural add-on / community visit via DMC (direct artisan purchases non-commissionable)","source":"https://www.tourismpanama.com/culture-cuisine/indigenous-communities/guna/","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Culture & Heritage (future)","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"cultural add-on / community visit via DMC (direct artisan purchases non-commissionable)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is San Blas safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes. The US State Department Level 2 advisory (reissued September 23, 2024) names Guna Yala / San Blas in no Level 4 or Level 3 area — the L4 \"Do Not Travel\" zones are the Darién and parts of the Mosquito Gulf, both distinct from the comarca, and there is no maritime or boat-crossing restriction affecting San Blas. Freely bookable.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in San Blas?","a":"Remoteness, not crime. There is no hospital and, on most cays, no clinic; serious illness or injury means evacuation to Panama City or the US, which can exceed $50,000. Comprehensive travel + medevac insurance is a condition of going, not an option — and dengue/malaria risk is year-round.","source":"smartraveller.gov.au, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the boat crossings and the 4x4 access road dangerous?","a":"Manageable but weather-governed. Everything moves by open boat, so insist on worn life vests, a licensed captain, and a real forecast check; the Colombia passage is 24–52 hours at open sea with no turning back mid-crossing. The overland Cartí route is a steep, rain-sensitive mountain road needing a 4x4 (4–5 hours). Guided only.","source":"sanblasadventures.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Which San Blas islands are best for beaches and snorkeling?","a":"The outer Cayos Holandeses (Dutch Cays) are widely rated the best snorkeling in the archipelago, with healthy reef and cushion starfish on the flats. Isla Perro holds the signature shallow-shipwreck snorkel a few metres from shore, while the Cayos Limones lagoon (Isla Pelícano, of *Money Heist* fame) offers the easiest crystal-shallow day-trip.","source":"seasanblas.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is San Blas good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, if you want elemental over polished. The set-piece is a private or near-private sand-cay cabaña — hammock, palm, reef at the doorstep, no wifi — from ~$56–$100/night full-board, scaling up to a private crewed catamaran overnight. Expect solar power and often no running water: this is the Caribbean before anyone built a lobby on it.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What is the Panama-to-Cartagena sailing trip like?","a":"It''s a genuine passage, not a lagoon cruise. Three days threading the San Blas cays, then 24–52 hours of open-water crossing to Colombia; shared cabins run ~$525–$750 (meals + immigration paperwork included), private from ~$900+. Small boats have limited cabins and sell out weeks ahead for dry-season departures.","source":"sanblasadventures.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Who are the Guna, and how do I enter the comarca?","a":"You enter on Guna terms. The Guna are a matrilineal people who won semi-autonomy in the 1925 revolution and still govern by congress under saila leaders; entry means a passport check and a per-person cash fee (~$20/foreigner) at the Cartí checkpoint, with no ATMs on the islands. Buy reverse-appliqué molas direct from the women who sew them.","source":"ampatours.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Blas Islands (Guna Yala), Panama — Castaway Cays, Sailing & the Guna | TravelWell.World","search_language":"es-PA","local_keywords":["San Blas Guna Yala","islas San Blas Panamá","velero San Blas Cartagena","cómo llegar a San Blas desde Ciudad de Panamá","cabañas San Blas Guna Yala","molas guna","Cayos Holandeses"],"long_tail_en":["how to get to San Blas islands from Panama City","San Blas to Cartagena sailing trip","best San Blas islands for snorkeling","Isla Perro shipwreck snorkel","private catamaran charter San Blas","is San Blas Panama safe"],"hreflang":["en","es-PA"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"type":"private crewed catamaran","name":"ZENITH / CruiseSanBlas / Charter in San Blas","note":"the luxury vehicle in Guna Yala — no branded ultra property exists","earning":"private-charter / CLIA lane"},{"type":"Panama City bookend hotel","name":"American Trade Hotel (Casco Viejo, Small Luxury Hotels of the World)","note":"consortia/Virtuoso-adjacent luxury anchor for the city night","earning":"Fora / consortia hotel commission"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Blas / Guna Yala, Panama, Panama"},"geo":{"lat":9.57,"lng":-78.95}}'::jsonb, 95),
  ('san-cristobal-de-las-casas-mexico', '10S', 'San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico', 'Mexico', 'San Cristóbal de las Casas', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Chiapas (San Cristóbal & Palenque)', '{"culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_named_area_language":"US govt employees may travel to Tapachula (city limits, S/W of Hwy 200); may NOT travel to municipality of Ocozocoautla; may NOT travel to Southeastern Chiapas polygon (Guatemala border Pacific->Netzahualcoyotl->Ocosingo->El Ocote->San Francisco Pujiltic->Mapastepec, E/N of Hwy 200). San Cristobal / Tuxtla / Chiapa de Corzo fall OUTSIDE named boundaries.","gate_decision":"BOOK WITH WARNING","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","consent_flow":{"disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live advisory + traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"content_only":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Tuxtla Gutierrez TGZ (Angel Albino Corzo Intl) ~77km / ~1h05-1h30 to San Cristobal via Hwy 190/190D; corridor outside restricted zone","road_safety_flag":"Hwy 199 San Cristobal<->Palenque via Ocosingo: reported armed robbery (mostly night) + CNTE blockades — daytime-only, guided/private transfer","altitude":"~2200m, mild","water":"bottled/purified only","dengue":"lowland concern (Palenque/jungle/canyon), not highland city","founder_attorney_flag":"consent-flow wording pending compliance-attorney sign-off; re-verify advisory before each fire and before live checkout"},"timing":{"peak":["Nov-Apr dry season","Dia de Muertos (Oct 31-Nov 2)","Semana Santa (2026: Mar 29-Apr 5)"],"inflection":"6-10 weeks pre-peak; boutique tier sells 8-12 weeks out","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (dry-season fire ~mid-Sep; Dia de Muertos fire ~early-mid Oct; Semana Santa 2026 fire ~early-mid Mar) — proceeds with mandatory L3 disclosure","off_season":"May-Oct green/rainy value window; culture fully accessible year-round; highland climate never hot"},"jewels":[{"name":"Andadores + Templo de Santo Domingo + Museo del Ámbar","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"city walking tour + hotel + shopping affiliate (live behind BWW)","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"city walking tour + hotel + shopping affiliate (live behind BWW)"},{"name":"San Juan Chamula syncretic church","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided community day tour ~US$65pp (live); community fee non-commissionable","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/san-juan-chamula-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"guided community day tour ~US$65pp (live); community fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Zinacantán weaving co-op","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Chamula+Zinacantán combo tour + co-op purchase (live)","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/zinacantan-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"Chamula+Zinacantán combo tour + co-op purchase (live)"},{"name":"Kakaw Museo del Cacao + café/chocolate culture","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"food/cultural experience affiliate + retail","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"food/cultural experience affiliate + retail"},{"name":"Chiapa de Corzo (UNESCO / Pueblo Mágico)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"paired with Sumidero day tour (DMC/affiliate, live)","source":"https://www.viator.com/Chiapas-attractions/Sumidero-Canyon-National-Park/d5506-a14134","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"paired with Sumidero day tour (DMC/affiliate, live)"},{"name":"Sumidero Canyon boat cruise","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided boat tour commissionable (live); park/boat federal fee non-commissionable","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","hook":"2-hour open-boat cruise — life jackets, seated ride, weather-dependent; low risk with licensed operators from Chiapa de Corzo. Guided","si":"expedition","blurb":"2-hour open-boat cruise — life jackets, seated ride, weather-dependent; low risk with licensed operators from Chiapa de Corzo. Guided","commission":"guided boat tour commissionable (live); park/boat federal fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Lagos de Montebello","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"guided long-day tour DMC (live) — keep to established tourist route near border","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"guided long-day tour DMC (live) — keep to established tourist route near border"},{"name":"El Chiflón waterfalls","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided day tour DMC/affiliate (live) + entrance non-commissionable","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","si":"expedition","commission":"guided day tour DMC/affiliate (live) + entrance non-commissionable"},{"name":"El Arcotete / Rancho Nuevo","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"local guide/transfer affiliate + entrance (live)","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"local guide/transfer affiliate + entrance (live)"},{"name":"Temazcal + boutique-casa spa evenings","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"hotel + spa package direct/DMC (live)","source":"http://www.casadelalmahotelboutiqueandspa.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","when":"year-round","commission":"hotel + spa package direct/DMC (live)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is San Cristóbal safe to visit given the Level 3 advisory?","a":"Yes, with an informed booking. Chiapas is US State Dept Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel,\" but the advisory names its danger away from San Cristóbal — the restricted Southeastern Chiapas polygon terminates at Ocosingo (~65 km east) and the one banned municipality is Ocozocoautla. San Cristóbal, Tuxtla and Chiapa de Corzo sit outside those boundaries, reached by air via Tuxtla Gutiérrez (TGZ, ~1 hr). TravelWell books it behind the full Level 3 disclosure.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for — is the road dangerous?","a":"The connective road is the risk, not the city. Highway 199 between San Cristóbal and Palenque via Ocosingo has reported armed robberies (predominantly at night) plus periodic CNTE union blockades that usually cause only short delays. The rule is daytime-only overland travel with a vetted guide or private transfer, never a night self-drive; the city center itself is pedestrian-comfortable by day.","source":"aboutsancristobal.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are San Juan Chamula and Zinacantán, and how do I visit respectfully?","a":"They are living Tzotzil Maya villages, 10 km out, and a guide is effectively mandatory. Chamula''s church is a pine-needle-floored space of Maya-Catholic fusion with ritual healings day and night and a strict no-photography rule inside; Zinacantán (99% Indigenous) is a backstrap-loom weaving town with a women''s co-op. Pay the community fees and follow a guide who knows the etiquette.","source":"wandersmiles.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is there to do in the city itself?","a":"Walk the pedestrian andadores — Real de Guadalupe and the Andador Eclesiástico — between two hillside churches. The Templo de Santo Domingo has Chiapas''s most elaborate carved pink facade with a Tzotzil/Tzeltal textile market at its churchyard, and the Museo del Ámbar (in the ex-convent of La Merced) shows amber with 25-million-year-old inclusions, alongside a strong Chiapas-coffee and cacao café culture.","source":"randomtrip.net, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is Sumidero Canyon, and is it worth it?","a":"Yes — it''s the region''s signature nature outing. A 2-hour open-boat cruise from the UNESCO colonial town of Chiapa de Corzo runs ~32 km beneath canyon walls up to ~1,000 m, past waterfalls and wildlife. It''s a low-risk daytime trip with licensed operators — life vests on, weather-dependent.","source":"voyagemexique.info, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is San Cristóbal a good base for a quiet, cultured couple''s trip?","a":"Yes — it''s cultured romance, not resort romance. At 2,200 m the highland evenings ask for a sweater; boutique colonial casas like Hotel Bö and Casa del Alma offer temazcal spa culture and courtyard dinners along cobblestone andadores. Come in the dry season (Nov–April), with crisp 18–24°C days, blue skies and minimal rain.","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Does the altitude affect visitors?","a":"Only mildly. At ~2,200 m some travelers feel light shortness of breath or a disturbed first night''s sleep, but it is not a serious altitude risk — hydrate and ease into exertion on day one. Drink bottled water only; dengue is a lowland concern (Palenque, the canyon), not the cool highland city.","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico: Highland Chiapas, Maya Culture & Sumidero Canyon | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San Cristóbal de las Casas","Cañón del Sumidero","San Juan Chamula","Zinacantán tejido","Lagos de Montebello","El Chiflón cascadas","hoteles boutique San Cristóbal","mejor época para viajar a Chiapas","es seguro San Cristóbal de las Casas"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"San Cristóbal de las Casas"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Hotel Bö","tier":"design-luxury boutique (not global 5-star)","earning":"Fora/Virtuoso consortia commission where participating; else bedbank/OTA","mor":true},{"name":"Casa del Alma Hotel Boutique & Spa","tier":"upper-mid spa boutique","earning":"consortia/agency commission or bedbank","mor":true},{"name":"Hotel Na Bolom","tier":"mid heritage/character","earning":"direct/OTA thin commission, high narrative value","mor":true},{"name":"Private-DMC program (Plan South America / bespoke)","tier":"ultra ground handle incl. private charter SC<->Palenque ~40min","earning":"MoR on itinerary not bed","mor":true}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":16.737,"lng":-92.6376}}'::jsonb, 96),
  ('san-ignacio-belize', '10S', 'San Ignacio / Cayo, Belize', 'Belize', 'Belize''s inland adventure capital **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Belize', '{"expedition","culture","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Base for Actun Tunichil Muknal (ATM) — a guided-only Maya sacrificial cave holding the calcified ''Crystal Maiden'' skeleton near San Ignacio, Cayo District.","Xunantunich''s El Castillo (~40 m) is Belize''s 2nd-tallest structure; reached by a hand-cranked Mopan River ferry ~20 min from town.","Caracol''s Caana pyramid (141 ft / 43 m) is Belize''s tallest structure; access via military-escorted convoy from Douglas D''Silva Forest Station (~9 am) due to Guatemala-border proximity.","Blancaneaux Lodge, a ~20-room hideaway in the Mountain Pine Ridge, was bought by Francis Ford Coppola in the early 1980s and opened to guests in 1993.","BZE (Belize International) to San Ignacio is a ~2-hour drive west on the Western/George Price Highway; the Cayo caves are accessible year-round."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (verify)","hospital":"San Ignacio Community Hospital (local); trauma to Belize City (~2 hrs) or air-medical evac to Belize City / Guatemala City (verify)","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for the country (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance), pulled live, plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"state_dept_carveout":"only Southside Belize City restricted; Cayo open","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"BZE -> San Ignacio ~2 hr drive, Western/George Price Highway; regional airstrip Maya Flats (verify)","guatemala_border_note":"Caracol requires military-escorted convoy; Xunantunich near border — disclose, verify current","malaria":"CDC: malaria a risk in SOME parts of Belize; treat mainland jungle as potential risk, advise travel-medicine consult","dengue":"present; mosquito-bite avoidance essential","vaccines":"Hepatitis A (all 1+), typhoid (rural/smaller-city) recommended","water":"bottled/treated only; avoid swimming in fresh unchlorinated water (leptospirosis) — ATM/cave-tubing are unavoidable-immersion guided activities","founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on the BOOK WITH WARNING bin (Four-Bin v3): full verbatim live US State Dept advisory disclosed + acknowledged at booking; only Southside Belize City is the named danger"},"timing":{"curve_shape":"dry-season inland spike (cave/road passability), not beach-weather driven","peak":"Dec-Apr dry season; Dec-Jan crowd/price peak; Feb-Mar balanced sweet spot","green_season":"Jun-Nov wet; caves accessible year-round and especially evocative Jun-Oct at high water; rates drop","hurricane_overlay":"Jun-Nov; Sep-Oct highest risk; direct Belize landfalls historically infrequent","fire_date":"~2026-11-20 (primary, dry-season ramp); secondary pulse ~late May (green-season value)","sharpen_note":"season boundaries drift; confirm cave-tour operating status + road passability on live operator advisories before each fire date"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Actun Tunichil Muknal (ATM) — Crystal Maiden","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"licensed DMC / lodge tour desk (~$164 pp)","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Actun_Tunichil_Muknal","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC / lodge tour desk (~$164 pp)"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Cave-tubing (Caves Branch / Cayo)","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC day-tour + lodge bundle","source":"https://www.pacztours.net/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC day-tour + lodge bundle"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Barton Creek Cave (canoe-through)","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"licensed DMC tour","source":"https://www.pacztours.net/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Paddled by canoe through a river cave with Maya archaeological remains — guided only","si":"expedition","blurb":"Paddled by canoe through a river cave with Maya archaeological remains — guided only","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC tour"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Mountain Pine Ridge + Rio On Pools + Rio Frio Cave + Big Rock Falls","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC 4x4 day tour / lodge-based","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/jungle-lodges-belize/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC 4x4 day tour / lodge-based"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Horseback riding (Macal/Mopan valleys)","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"lodge activity / DMC","source":"https://chaacreek.com/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"lodge activity / DMC"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Xunantunich + El Castillo + hand-cranked ferry","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC half-day / lodge tour","source":"https://www.nayawalk.com/belize/xunantunich/","hook":"The Classic Maya city sits near the Belize–Guatemala border","si":"culture","blurb":"The Classic Maya city sits near the Belize–Guatemala border","commission":"DMC half-day / lodge tour"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Caracol — Caana (Belize''s tallest structure)","tier":"premier","commission_path":"licensed DMC full-day + convoy logistics","source":"https://trans-americas.com/caracol-archaeological-site-belize/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Reached only by military-escorted convoy from the Douglas D''Silva Forest Station because of Guatemala-border proximity","si":"culture","blurb":"Reached only by military-escorted convoy from the Douglas D''Silva Forest Station because of Guatemala-border proximity","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC full-day + convoy logistics"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Cahal Pech (walking distance from town)","tier":"essential","commission_path":"self-guided fee / add-on guided walk","source":"https://www.stleonardsbelize.com/belize-tours/xunantunich-cahal-pech-tour","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"self-guided fee / add-on guided walk"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Tikal day-trip (Guatemala)","tier":"premier","commission_path":"licensed DMC full-day cross-border","source":"https://www.pacztours.net/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC full-day cross-border"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Green Iguana Conservation Project","tier":"essential","commission_path":"in-town lodge activity / affiliate","source":"https://www.sanignaciobelize.com/green-iguana-conservation-project/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Romance & Nature","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"in-town lodge activity / affiliate"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Belize Botanic Gardens at du Plooy''s","tier":"essential","commission_path":"lodge stay / day visit / bedbank","source":"https://www.sanignaciobelize.com/","si":"Romance & Nature","commission":"lodge stay / day visit / bedbank"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Chaa Creek Butterfly Farm + Macal River canoe","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"lodge stay + activity","source":"https://chaacreek.com/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Romance & Nature","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"lodge stay + activity"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Spanish Lookout (Mennonite community)","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC add-on / self-drive","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/belize/western-belize/san-ignacio-cayo/attractions/green-iguana-conservation-project/a/poi-sig/460812/358218","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Romance & Nature","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC add-on / self-drive"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the ATM cave tour like, and do you need a guide?","a":"It is the apex Cayo adventure and it is guided-only by law — you cannot legally enter Actun Tunichil Muknal without a licensed operator. Expect a ~45-minute jungle trek with multiple river crossings, a swim into the cave mouth, wading a shallow underground river in total darkness, and tight climbs; ~3 hours inside. Cameras have been banned since a 2012 incident cracked a ~1,000-year-old skull.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"How do you visit Caracol and Xunantunich?","a":"Differently. Caracol — whose Caana pyramid (141 ft/43 m) is Belize''s tallest structure — requires a military-escorted convoy from the Douglas D''Silva Forest Station (muster ~9 am, return ~2 pm) because it sits near the porous Guatemala border. Xunantunich is easier: a 20-minute drive and a hand-cranked Mopan River ferry to El Castillo, ~40 m and the country''s second-tallest structure.","source":"trans-americas.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is San Ignacio good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — for jungle romance rather than beach. The luxury lodge belt is world-class: Coppola''s Blancaneaux Lodge (~20 rooms, Mountain Pine Ridge waterfalls), the 500-acre Green Globe reserve at Chaa Creek (founded 1981, with butterfly farm, spa and Macal River canoeing), and Ka''ana''s plunge-pool villas. Plunge-pool casitas, canopy dinners and waterfall spas define the market.","source":"chaacreek.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is San Ignacio safe right now?","a":"Yes, with the standard disclosure. Belize is at US State Dept Level 3 (reissued June 18, 2026, code C/Crime only), but the only named-restricted area is Southside Belize City; San Ignacio and Cayo are not named and sit ~110 km — roughly a 2-hour drive — inland from it. Disclose the overall L3 clearly and stay in-zone.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-06-18","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cayo?","a":"Water, wildlife and inland health, not urban crime. CDC advises avoiding swimming in fresh, unchlorinated water (leptospirosis), yet ATM and cave-tubing involve unavoidable river immersion, so treat them as guided-only informed-consent activities; high water after heavy rain periodically closes the caves. CDC also states malaria is a risk in some parts of Belize — treat the mainland jungle as potential risk and get a travel-medicine consult; dengue is present.","source":"wwwnc.cdc.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the ATM cave tour dangerous?","a":"It is physically demanding but safe as a licensed, guided activity — there is no legal or safe self-tour option. The tour requires \"good to very good\" fitness for river fordings, swimming into the cave, and tight passages and climbs in the upper chambers, with a minimum height of ~40 inches. Cave-tubing and Barton Creek Cave are likewise licensed-guide-required, with rising-water hazard after rain.","source":"chaacreek.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Ignacio & Cayo, Belize: ATM Cave, Xunantunich, Caracol & Jungle Lodges | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Belize''s inland adventure capital — swim into the Crystal Maiden''s cave, climb Caracol and Xunantunich, sleep in Coppola''s jungle hideaway. Guided-only cave tours, luxury eco-lodges, how to travel Cayo well.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["San Ignacio Belize","Cayo District adventure","ATM cave tour","Actun Tunichil Muknal Crystal Maiden","Xunantunich hand-cranked ferry","Caracol military convoy","Blancaneaux Lodge Belize","cave tubing Belize","best jungle lodges San Ignacio","is Cayo Belize safe 2026"],"hreflang":["en","es-419 (optional)"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","Culture & Heritage (future)","romance"],"ultra":[{"name":"Blancaneaux Lodge","why":"~20-room Coppola hideaway, Mountain Pine Ridge, waterfall pools","earning_path":"Family Coppola Hideaways direct + consortia/Fora lane","mor":"direct-to-lodge","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Ka''ana Resort","why":"18 suites/villas, private plunge pools, boutique 17-acre estate","earning_path":"consortia/Fora + direct","mor":"direct","tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"The Lodge at Chaa Creek","why":"500-acre Green Globe reserve, Macal River, spa, villas","earning_path":"direct + advisor consortia","mor":"direct/AOR","tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"Gaïa Riverlodge","why":"Small Luxury Hotels of the World; 16 cabanas atop Five Sisters Falls, hydropowered","earning_path":"SLH channel + consortia","mor":"SLH/direct","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Table Rock Jungle Lodge","why":"intimate boutique Macal-riverfront cabañas","earning_path":"direct commission","mor":"direct","tier":"comfort"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"San Ignacio / Cayo, Belize, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":17.1598,"lng":-89.0714}}'::jsonb, 97),
  ('san-jose-costa-rica', '10S', 'San José & the Central Valley', 'Costa Rica', 'Volcanoes, coffee estates, whitewater **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Costa Rica', '{"culture","expedition"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["SJO Juan Santamaría is Costa Rica''s primary international gateway, 20km NW of downtown; record high season Nov 2025–Apr 2026 with 3,215,208 intl passengers (+7.9% YoY).","Central Valley sits at ~1,150m ''eternal-spring'' highland climate — low dengue, mild year-round, tap water potable.","Pre-Columbian Gold Museum holds ~1,600 gold pieces (500–1500 AD) beneath Plaza de la Cultura beside the Teatro Nacional.","Poás & Irazú volcanoes are both same-day from San José; Irazú tops 3,432m with both oceans visible on clear mornings; Poás active with dynamic-access timed entry.","Doka Estate is Costa Rica''s oldest continuously operating coffee plantation, ~1.5hrs from the capital."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Hospital Clínica Bíblica (largest private, 1929, JCI, 24/7 heliport evac) + Hospital CIMA (US-affiliated, JCI) — San José is the national medical & evac hub","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"SJO — Juan Santamaría International (primary international gateway)","water":"potable in Central Valley / San José"},"timing":{"demand_type":"derivative","tracks":"onward_anchor_demand (Manuel Antonio / Arenal / Monteverde / Guanacaste)","peak":"mid-December–April (dry season) + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","inflection_curve_start":"early-to-mid October (itinerary-locking wave)","fire_date":"late September (curve-start minus 1–2 weeks; gateway-bed + transfer window ahead of anchors)","shoulder_green":"May–November","booking_lead":"gateway bed short-lead (days–2wk); underlying anchor trip long-lead (2–6mo)","events":["Festival de la Luz (2nd Sat Dec, San José)","Día Nacional del Boyero (2nd Sun Mar, Escazú)","Juan Santamaría Day (Apr 11)"],"confidence":"modeled — sharpen on live gateway/transfer tracking vs anchor curves"},"jewels":[{"name":"Teatro Nacional de Costa Rica","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","commission_path":"affiliate guided-tour / DMC city tour","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/costa-rica/san-jose/attractions/museo-de-oro-precolombino-y-numismatica/a/poi-sig/425769/358357 (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the 1897 neoclassical opera house on Plaza de la Cultura, the country''s proudest single building; guided tour + café","si":"culture","blurb":"the 1897 neoclassical opera house on Plaza de la Cultura, the country''s proudest single building; guided tour + café","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"affiliate guided-tour / DMC city tour","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Museo del Oro Precolombino (Gold Museum)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","commission_path":"non-commissionable entry wrapped in commissionable DMC/affiliate city walk","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/costa-rica/san-jose/attractions/museo-de-oro-precolombino-y-numismatica/a/poi-sig/425769/358357 (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"~1,600 gold pieces, 500–1500 AD, subterranean under Plaza de la Cultura beside the Teatro","si":"culture","blurb":"~1,600 gold pieces, 500–1500 AD, subterranean under Plaza de la Cultura beside the Teatro","when":"year-round","commission":"non-commissionable entry wrapped in commissionable DMC/affiliate city walk","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Museo del Jade","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","commission_path":"entry non-commissionable, wrapped in DMC/affiliate city tour","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g309293-d10319348-Reviews-Museo_del_Jade-San_Jose_San_Jose_Metro_Province_of_San_Jose.html (Accessed 2026-07-06)","t