 Mediterranean, Latin fusion, craft beer","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"food-tour affiliate + commissionable dinner reservations","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Poás Volcano National Park (crater rim)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"commissionable guided day-tour wrapping non-commissionable SINAC entry","source":"https://costaricatravelblog.com/poas-volcano-national-park-reservations/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"active crater, dynamic-access timed entry, one of the world''s most accessible active volcanoes; classically paired with Doka coffee","si":"expedition","blurb":"active crater, dynamic-access timed entry, one of the world''s most accessible active volcanoes; classically paired with Doka coffee","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable guided day-tour wrapping non-commissionable SINAC entry","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Irazú Volcano National Park + Cartago","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"commissionable combo day-tour","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/irazu-volcano-cartago-day-trip-from-san-jose-2026-complete-guide.htm (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the highest volcano in the country, turquoise Diego-de-la-Haya crater lake, both-oceans-on-a-clear-morning, paired with the Basílica de los Ángeles in Cartago. Half-day $45–85, combined $60–95","si":"expedition","blurb":"the highest volcano in the country, turquoise Diego-de-la-Haya crater lake, both-oceans-on-a-clear-morning, paired with the Basílica de los Ángeles in Cartago. Half-day $45–85, combined $60–95","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable combo day-tour","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"La Paz Waterfall Gardens","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"commissionable day-pass + tour","source":"https://mytanfeet.com/activities/la-paz-waterfall-gardens/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","hook":"5 waterfalls, cloud-forest trails, 100+ animal wildlife refuge, ~3.5 km of paved trails; the crowd-pleaser day-park, often stacked with Poás+Doka","si":"expedition","blurb":"5 waterfalls, cloud-forest trails, 100+ animal wildlife refuge, ~3.5 km of paved trails; the crowd-pleaser day-park, often stacked with Poás+Doka","commission":"commissionable day-pass + tour","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Pacuare River whitewater (day or overnight lodge)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"commissionable operator day-trip; overnight lodge = higher-margin package","source":"https://mytanfeet.com/activities/white-water-rafting-at-rio-pacuare-costa-rica/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Class III–IV rainforest-gorge rafting from the metro; the overnight-lodge version is the premium upsell","si":"expedition","blurb":"Class III–IV rainforest-gorge rafting from the metro; the overnight-lodge version is the premium upsell","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable operator day-trip; overnight lodge = higher-margin package","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Orosi Valley + Lankester Botanical Gardens","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"commissionable combo day-tour","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/san-jose/tours/Irazu-Orosi-Lankester.php (Accessed 2026-07-06)","hook":"colonial Orosi + 800+ orchid species under University of Costa Rica protection; often the third leg of the Irazú day","si":"expedition","blurb":"colonial Orosi + 800+ orchid species under University of Costa Rica protection; often the third leg of the Irazú day","commission":"commissionable combo day-tour","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Doka Estate coffee tour","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","commission_path":"commissionable tour (Viator/ANYWHERE/DMC)","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/san-jose-coffee-tours-2026-doka-estate-best-farms.htm (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Costa Rica''s oldest continuously operating coffee plantation, 70-hectare farm, ~1.5 hrs from San José, seedling-to-cup with bilingual guides; classic ~$25–35, premium cupping ~$65","si":"culture","blurb":"Costa Rica''s oldest continuously operating coffee plantation, 70-hectare farm, ~1.5 hrs from San José, seedling-to-cup with bilingual guides; classic ~$25–35, premium cupping ~$65","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable tour (Viator/ANYWHERE/DMC)","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Café Britt coffee tour","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","commission_path":"commissionable tour","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/san-jose-coffee-tours-2026-doka-estate-best-farms.htm (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the polished, theatrical coffee-education show near Heredia; standard ~$32, barista experience ~$75. The entertainment-first alternative to Doka''s authenticity-first","si":"culture","blurb":"the polished, theatrical coffee-education show near Heredia; standard ~$32, barista experience ~$75. The entertainment-first alternative to Doka''s authenticity-first","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable tour","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Sarchí oxcart crafts","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","commission_path":"commissionable combo day-tour + retail","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/san-jose/tours/Poas-Volcano-Doka-Coffee-Plantation-and-La-Paz.php (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the town that hand-paints the carreta, Costa Rica''s national-symbol oxcart; the world''s largest oxcart and the artisan workshops. Usually stacked with Poás/Doka/Grecia","si":"culture","blurb":"the town that hand-paints the carreta, Costa Rica''s national-symbol oxcart; the world''s largest oxcart and the artisan workshops. Usually stacked with Poás/Doka/Grecia","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable combo day-tour + retail","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is San José worth staying a night, or just an airport?","a":"Worth a night. It''s the front door, not the destination — but the Pre-Columbian Gold Museum (~1,600 pieces, beside the Teatro Nacional), a three-museum pass (~$33), and the Barrio Escalante restaurant row give a genuine half-to-full day of culture-and-coffee substance.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can you day-trip Poás and Irazú volcanoes from San José?","a":"Yes — both are same-day from the capital. Irazú tops 3,432 m with both oceans visible on a clear morning; Poás runs a dynamic-access, online-only timed-entry model via SINAC, so go guided to absorb the timed-entry and closure logistics.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where is SJO airport and how busy does it get?","a":"Juan Santamaría (SJO) is Costa Rica''s primary international gateway, 20 km northwest of downtown in Alajuela. It just set a record, handling 3,215,208 international passengers between Nov 2025 and Apr 5 2026 — up 7.9% year-over-year — so book gateway beds and transfers ahead of the dry-season wave.","source":"ticotimes.net, 2026-07-06","si_tag":null},{"q":"Is San José safe right now?","a":"Yes, with city smarts. It''s U.S. Level 2 (updated Apr 2, 2026) — the same tier as France, Italy and the UK. The real story is urban petty crime: downtown pickpocketing and bag-snatching (Mercado Central, bus terminals, crowded plazas), plus rental-car and beach break-ins. Use licensed red taxis or a rideshare app, and don''t flash valuables.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is it safe to visit Poás, an active volcano?","a":"Yes, under the park''s gas-safety controls. Poás actively vents SO₂ and H₂S, so access is dynamic: online-only tickets, 56 visitors per 30-min shift (8:00 am–2:00 pm last entry), crater-viewpoint time capped at ~20 minutes, and real-time monitoring triggers same-day closures. Go guided and confirm day-of status.","source":"costaricatravelblog.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"If something goes wrong in Costa Rica, is medical care nearby?","a":"Reassuringly, yes — San José IS the national medical and evacuation hub. Hospital Clínica Bíblica (founded 1929, JCI-accredited, 24/7, with an on-site heliport for evac) and the US-affiliated Hospital CIMA are both in the metro, so serious care and the evac hub are right here.","source":"internationalinsurance.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San José & Costa Rica''s Central Valley: Volcanoes, Coffee Tours & the Gateway to Pura Vida | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Poás & Irazú volcanoes, Doka & Café Britt coffee estates, the Gold & Jade museums, and Pacuare whitewater — all day-trippable from SJO. The accurate guide to Costa Rica''s Central Valley gateway. TravelWell.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San José Costa Rica","Volcán Poás tour","tour de café Costa Rica","Volcán Irazú desde San José","Museo del Oro Precolombino","rafting río Pacuare un día","hoteles cerca del aeropuerto Juan Santamaría","Barrio Escalante dónde comer"],"long_tail_en":["things to do in San José Costa Rica one day","Poás Volcano tour from San José 2026","Irazú Volcano Cartago day trip","best coffee tour near San José Doka vs Café Britt","Pacuare River rafting day trip from San José","where to stay near SJO airport Costa Rica"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["culture_heritage","expedition"],"ultra":[{"name":"Finca Rosa Blanca","type":"coffee-estate boutique","location":"Santa Bárbara de Heredia","tier":"ultra (valley)","mor":"brand-direct/DMC net rate","consortia":"sold via Jacada/Lightfoot luxury operators; Virtuoso not independently confirmed — verify","fora_lane":true},{"name":"Xandari Resort & Spa","type":"hillside villa-suite eco-boutique","location":"Alajuela","tier":"premier–ultra (valley)","mor":"brand-direct/DMC net rate","consortia":"not confirmed — verify","fora_lane":true},{"name":"Hotel Grano de Oro","type":"tropical-Victorian casona boutique","location":"San José city","tier":"premier (city)","mor":"brand-direct/DMC","consortia":"not confirmed — verify","fora_lane":true},{"name":"Costa Rica Marriott Hotel Hacienda Belén","type":"hacienda-style branded luxury resort","location":"La Asunción (near SJO)","tier":"premium–premier (airport)","mor":"brand-direct (Marriott)","consortia":"Marriott STARS/Luminous where eligible","fora_lane":true}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"San José & the Central Valley, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":9.9281,"lng":-84.0907}}'::jsonb, 98)
insert into public.destinations (id, region_code, name, country, line, status, depth, img, sub_region, si, feel, tier_range, price_band, draw_rank, data, position) values
  ('san-jose-del-cabo-mexico', '10S', 'San José del Cabo', 'Mexico', '*If it''s a lantern-lit gallery street, a Blue Flag', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"romance","expedition","culture","ocean"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Gallery District Art Walk runs Thursdays 5–9 pm, November–June, free (Source: ivanguaderrama.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Estero de San José is the only freshwater coastal lagoon in BCS, a State Ecological Reserve/IBA with 270+ bird species (Source: mexicobirdingtrail.org, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Playa Palmilla is Blue Flag and one of the few consistently swimmable Corridor beaches (Source: casanatalia.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Whale season mid-Dec–mid-Apr, humpback + gray, ~90–95% peak sightings (Source: visitloscabos.travel, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Hurricane peak Aug–Oct, September historically most active for Los Cabos (Source: mexiconewsdaily.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"H+ Los Cabos (Km 24.5 Transpeninsular, 24/7 ER); AmeriMed (San José + CSL, bilingual 24/7); Blue Medical/BlueNet (24/7 ER); air-evac to US for serious cases","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required"},"timing":{"peak":"November–April (dry season, whale-watching, Art Walk)","shoulder":"May–June & late October","green":"July–September into early October (hot, hurricane/chubasco)","booking_lead":"3–6+ months for peak ultra/villa; advance dining reservations Dec–Mar","off_season_specials":"Green-season warm-water ocean + spa value; disclose storm risk + insurance","event_peaks":"Christmas/New Year, Semana Santa, whale Jan–Mar, Art Walk Thu Nov–Jun","campaign_start":"Late summer/early fall for Nov–Apr peak; late spring for green-season value"},"jewels":[{"name":"Gallery District Art Walk","si_tag":"Culture & Arts","status":"future","hook":"Thursday-night open-gallery cobblestone stroll, free, Nov–Jun","bookable_category":"free / bundle with dining","tier":"essential","commission_path":"adjacent dining/experience or hotel package","source":"https://www.ivanguaderrama.com/san-jose-del-cabo-art-walk-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Culture & Arts","blurb":"Thursday-night open-gallery cobblestone stroll, free, Nov–Jun","when":"year-round","commission":"adjacent dining/experience or hotel package","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Estero de San José birding","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"270+ species freshwater lagoon reserve, endangered Belding''s Yellowthroat","bookable_category":"guided birding tour","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate / DMC","source":"http://mexicobirdingtrail.org/plan-a-trip/san-jose-del-cabo-estuary/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"270+ species freshwater lagoon reserve, endangered Belding''s Yellowthroat","when":"November–April","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Whale-watching (Corridor)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Humpback + gray whale tours, ~90–95% peak sightings","bookable_category":"panga/catamaran tour","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate / Amstar DMC","source":"https://www.cabo-adventures.com/en/tour/whale-watching-in-cabo (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"Humpback + gray whale tours, ~90–95% peak sightings","commission":"activity affiliate / Amstar DMC","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Playa Palmilla swim/snorkel","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"Blue Flag, protected swim beach fronting One&Only","bookable_category":"free beach + snorkel add-ons","tier":"essential","commission_path":"activity affiliate","source":"https://www.casanatalia.com/nearby-attractions/san-jose-del-cabo-beaches/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"ocean","blurb":"Blue Flag, protected swim beach fronting One&Only","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Corridor golf + spa day","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"27-hole/championship golf + resort spas for couples","bookable_category":"tee times + spa via resort/DMC","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC / resort","source":"https://www.oneandonlyresorts.com/palmilla (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","blurb":"27-hole/championship golf + resort spas for couples","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC / resort","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"Where''s the top end for a honeymoon in San José?","a":"San José/Palmilla is the branded-ultra spine of Los Cabos: One&Only Palmilla (the 1956-origin icon, 27-hole golf), Zadún (a Ritz-Carlton Reserve, 115 villas), Chileno Bay and Esperanza (Auberge). It''s the quiet, composed counterweight to Cabo San Lucas'' nightlife.","source":"virtuoso.com / guide.michelin.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When can I see whales, and is the estuary worth it?","a":"Whale season is mid-December to mid-April with ~90–95% sightings at peak (mother-calf pairs Jan–Feb). For nature on land, the Estero de San José — BCS''s only freshwater coastal lagoon and an Important Bird Area — holds 270+ bird species, best at dawn.","source":"visitloscabos.travel / mexicobirdingtrail.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Which San José beaches can I actually swim?","a":"Very few — most open Corridor beaches have strong currents and are not swim-safe. The reliable exception is Blue Flag Playa Palmilla, with a protected swimming area; Chileno and Santa María are the other Corridor swim beaches.","source":"casanatalia.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"What is the Art Walk, and when is it?","a":"Every Thursday evening, 5–9 pm, November through June, the Gallery District opens more than a dozen galleries along the cobblestone streets around Álvaro Obregón, with music and refreshments — and it''s free. Book Art Walk-night dinner ahead Dec–March.","source":"ivanguaderrama.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is San José del Cabo safe right now?","a":"Yes — freely bookable. Baja California Sur is US State Dept Level 2 \"Exercise Increased Caution\" (May 29, 2026) and one of Mexico''s safer states, with modern private hospitals (H+ Los Cabos, AmeriMed) on the Corridor.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29 / loscabosguide.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The ocean and the weather, not crime. Most open San José beaches have dangerous rip currents — swim only at Blue Flag Palmilla or other designated coves — and hurricane season runs Jun–Nov, September historically worst. Carry trip insurance for green-season dates.","source":"casanatalia.com / mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San José del Cabo Travel Guide — Art Walk, Whales & Blue Flag Beaches | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"The refined side of Los Cabos: Gallery District Art Walk, Estero San José birding, whale-watching, swim-safe Playa Palmilla, and branded-ultra resorts.","slug":"san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","primary_keyword":"San José del Cabo travel guide","long_tail":["San José del Cabo Art Walk Thursday","San José del Cabo vs Cabo San Lucas","Playa Palmilla swimming","whale watching San José del Cabo","luxury resorts San José del Cabo"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San José del Cabo","Art Walk San José del Cabo horarios","Estero de San José del Cabo aves","Playa Palmilla se puede nadar","avistamiento de ballenas Los Cabos","hoteles de lujo San José del Cabo"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"One&Only Palmilla","why_ultra":"Legendary 1956-origin 174-room Sea-of-Cortez retreat, 13 private-villa spa, 27-hole golf; Palmilla = San José","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"resort credit + upgrade + breakfast (verify current)","mor":true},{"name":"Chileno Bay Resort & Residences (Auberge)","why_ultra":"Auberge; Mykonos-white low-rise, football-field pool, swim-safe Chileno beach","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":true},{"name":"Esperanza, Auberge Resorts Collection","why_ultra":"Clifftop Corridor Auberge classic","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":true},{"name":"Viceroy Los Cabos","why_ultra":"Design-forward San José Corridor resort","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":true},{"name":"Zadún, a Ritz-Carlton Reserve","why_ultra":"San José coastline; 115 villas (many private-pool) + Residences, 2 championship courses, botanical park; 4th Reserve globally","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":true}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"San José del Cabo, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":23.0631,"lng":-109.7025}}'::jsonb, 99),
  ('san-juan-del-sur-nicaragua', '10S', 'San Juan del Sur, Nicaragua', 'Nicaragua', 'Pacific surf town in a horseshoe bay **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Nicaragua', '{"tropical","romance"}', '{}', '{"ultra"}', 'ultra', null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"118","emergency_ambulance":"128","emergency_fire":"115 / 911 (cell)","tourist_helpline":"101","us_embassy_managua":"+505-2252-7100","advisory_date":"2026-05-14","advisory_source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/nicaragua-travel-advisory.html","book_enabled":false,"bin":"NO SAFE ZONE (content-only)","redirect_eligible":true,"consent_flow":null,"founder_review_flag":"Do not enable Book path, consent flow, or commission until US advisory drops below Level 3 or a defensible carve-out is designated AND founder + compliance attorney sign off in writing. Re-run gate live before any status change.","trauma_note":"Quality care only in Managua (~2.5h+); local stabilization → Managua → likely US medevac; robust evacuation insurance prerequisite (content only)."},"timing":{"peak_surf_dry":"Nov–Apr (clean, offshore-groomed, learner-friendly)","peak_surf_wet":"May–Oct (bigger SE swells, intermediate-to-advanced)","peak_turtle_arribada":"Jul–Jan, peak Sep–Oct (~7 arribadas)","inflection":"May–Jun shoulder","fire_date":"held — pending advisory clearance + founder/attorney","off_season_note":"No dead season for content; Book path off by gate, not season"},"jewels":[{"name":"Playa Maderas","si_tag":"GEA-Surf","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://thesurfatlas.com/nicaragua-surf/playa-maderas-surf/","hook":"The signature wave and the signature sunset; a bay north of town with a fine A-frame, forgiving on small days, powerful on swell","si":"GEA-Surf","blurb":"The signature wave and the signature sunset; a bay north of town with a fine A-frame, forgiving on small days, powerful on swell","commission":"dormant","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Playa Hermosa","si_tag":"GEA-Surf","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://thesurfatlas.com/nicaragua-surf/san-juan-del-sur-surf/","hook":"Over a mile of open beach with multiple peaks, long walls, the odd barrel","si":"GEA-Surf","blurb":"Over a mile of open beach with multiple peaks, long walls, the odd barrel","commission":"dormant","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Cristo de la Misericordia viewpoint","si_tag":"Tropical/Romance","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nicaragua/southwestern-nicaragua/san-juan-del-sur/attractions/cristo-de-la-misericordia/a/poi-sig/1369205/358508","hook":"Roughly 24–25m of open-armed Christ on the northern headland, a short steep hike, 360° bay-and-Pacific panorama, open 8am–5pm, ~US$2 entry","si":"Tropical/Romance","blurb":"Roughly 24–25m of open-armed Christ on the northern headland, a short steep hike, 360° bay-and-Pacific panorama, open 8am–5pm, ~US$2 entry","commission":"dormant","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Playa Marsella","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://mangorosanicaragua.com/surfing-in-southern-nicaragua/","hook":"The gentler, family-tempered beach on the north road, home to beachfront boutique lodging and an easy day away from the town crowds","si":"Tropical/Beaches","blurb":"The gentler, family-tempered beach on the north road, home to beachfront boutique lodging and an easy day away from the town crowds","commission":"dormant","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"La Flor olive-ridley arribada","si_tag":"Wildlife/Tropical","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nicaragua/beaches-south-of-san-juan-del-sur/attractions/refugio-de-vida-silvestre-la-flor/a/poi-sig/1324287/1328451","hook":"~20km south of town; ~800 hectares; ~30,000 turtles a year across seven mass arribadas; eggs laid ~9pm–2am, Jul–Jan, peaking Sep–Oct; guided night tours only","si":"Wildlife/Tropical","blurb":"~20km south of town; ~800 hectares; ~30,000 turtles a year across seven mass arribadas; eggs laid ~9pm–2am, Jul–Jan, peaking Sep–Oct; guided night tours only","commission":"dormant","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Sunset catamaran (Pelican Eyes yacht)","si_tag":"romance","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/nicaragua/pelican_eyes.html","si":"romance","commission":"dormant"},{"name":"Sunday Funday pool crawl (context)","si_tag":"Culture/Nightlife","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.explorewithlora.com/sunday-funday-nicaragua/","hook":"Running since 2013 out of Pachamama Hostel, up to 500 travelers weekly across three-to-four venues; the defining backpacker ritual of San Juan del Sur","si":"Culture/Nightlife","blurb":"Running since 2013 out of Pachamama Hostel, up to 500 travelers weekly across three-to-four venues; the defining backpacker ritual of San Juan del Sur","commission":"dormant"}],"faq":null,"seo":{"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","meta_title":"San Juan del Sur, Nicaragua — Surf, Turtles & the Christ Statue | TravelWell","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-NI","long_tail_en":["san juan del sur surf season","playa maderas surf guide","la flor turtle nesting season","cristo de la misericordia hike","is san juan del sur safe 2026","san juan del sur sunset catamaran"],"local_keywords":["San Juan del Sur surf","Playa Maderas","tortugas La Flor","Cristo de la Misericordia mirador","Playa Hermosa olas","arribada tortugas Nicaragua"],"hreflang":["en","es-NI"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Aqua Wellness Resort","tier":"ultra-wellness","note":"secluded-cove treehouse villas, spa positioning","earning":"dormant"},{"name":"Pelican Eyes Resort & Spa","tier":"ultra-beach","note":"crescent-bay villas, 3 pools, Casa Tranquila Spa, sunset yacht","earning":"dormant","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/nicaragua/pelican_eyes.html"},{"name":"Casa Marsella","tier":"boutique-beachfront","note":"Playa Marsella beachfront boutique","earning":"dormant"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Juan del Sur, Nicaragua, Nicaragua"},"geo":{"lat":11.2528,"lng":-85.8703}}'::jsonb, 100),
  ('san-miguel-de-allende-mexico', '10S', 'San Miguel de Allende', 'Mexico', '*If it''s the moment your whole party goes quiet', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Guanajuato (San Miguel de Allende)', '{"romance","culture","culinary","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Repeatedly named ''Best Small City in the World'' (Condé Nast Traveler Readers'' Choice) (Source: luceroalvarez.com, Accessed 2026-07-05)","Mexico''s destination-wedding capital with a decades-deep planner/vendor ecosystem; venues 20–300 guests (Source: destinationweddings.com, Accessed 2026-07-05)","High-desert climate, 300+ days sun/yr, peak comfort Oct–May, ~1,900 m altitude (Source: destinationweddings.com, Accessed 2026-07-05)","UNESCO World Heritage historic town; Santuario de Atotonilco (''Sistine Chapel of the Americas'') ~15 min away (Source: viator.com, Accessed 2026-07-05)","Air access via BJX (Del Bajío/León, ~1.5 hr) and QRO (Querétaro, ~1 hr) (Source: rome2rio.com, Accessed 2026-07-05)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Hospital MAC San Miguel de Allende (2017; ER, ICU, neonatal ICU, 2 ORs, CT, MRI, ultrasound, ambulance); advanced trauma/cardiac evac to Querétaro (~1 hr) or León","advisory_level":"L3","book_enabled":true,"tourist_zone_carveout":"historic centers; no specific named carve-out — disclose plainly (softer than Jalisco)","air_access_verified":"BJX (Del Bajío/León) + QRO (Querétaro)","stay_in_zone_advisory":"Stay in the SMA tourist zone; risk is rural/highway south of Federal Hwy 45D (Celaya/Salamanca/Irapuato industrial-oil-theft corridor), not the historic center; do not self-drive southern-Guanajuato highways; use vetted transfers","mandatory_disclosure":"L3 ''Reconsider Travel'' state, no named tourist carve-out — disclose at booking","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","altitude":"~1,900 m (~6,200 ft) — mild AMS possible day 1–2; hydrate, pace alcohol","water":"bottled/purified only"},"timing":