x — studios, shops, cafés","bookable_category":"guided art walk","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate / DMC","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-san-miguel-de-allende-guanajuato/ (Accessed 2026-07-05)","si":"culture","blurb":"1902 cotton mill turned gallery/design complex — studios, shops, cafés","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Santuario de Atotonilco (UNESCO)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"''Sistine Chapel of the Americas'' — six chapels of floor-to-ceiling baroque murals, ~15 min north","bookable_category":"guided day trip (paired w/ Dolores)","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate / DMC (entry = non-commissionable)","source":"https://www.viator.com/San-Miguel-de-Allende-attractions/Santuario-de-Atotonilco/d26115-a102681 (Accessed 2026-07-05)","timing":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"''Sistine Chapel of the Americas'' — six chapels of floor-to-ceiling baroque murals, ~15 min north","when":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC (entry = non-commissionable)","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Tuesday market (Tianguis)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Sprawling local market — textiles, crafts, food","bookable_category":"guided market/shopping tour","tier":"essential","commission_path":"activity affiliate","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-san-miguel-de-allende-guanajuato/ (Accessed 2026-07-05)","timing":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Sprawling local market — textiles, crafts, food","when":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Guanajuato wine route (Viñedos San Miguel + Cuna de Tierra)","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"High-desert wineries; Cuna de Tierra is the state''s oldest","bookable_category":"wine-route tour + tasting + lunch","tier":"premier","commission_path":"activity affiliate / DMC","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/day-trips-from-san-miguel-de-allende/ (Accessed 2026-07-05)","timing":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"High-desert wineries; Cuna de Tierra is the state''s oldest","when":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Dolores Hidalgo — independence + nieves exóticas","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Birthplace of Mexican independence + famous exotic ice creams (tequila, avocado, shrimp)","bookable_category":"day trip (paired w/ Atotonilco)","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate / DMC","source":"https://epicureanexpats.com/dolores-hidalgo-and-atotonilco/ (Accessed 2026-07-05)","timing":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"Birthplace of Mexican independence + famous exotic ice creams (tequila, avocado, shrimp)","when":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"La Gruta hot springs","si_tag":"Wellness","status":"future","hook":"Thermal pools reached through a lit volcanic cave tunnel, ~20 min out","bookable_category":"entry + transfer or spa package","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate / DMC","source":"https://mexicotravel.blog/la-gruta-spa-hot-springs-san-miguel-de-allende/ (Accessed 2026-07-05)","si":"wellness","blurb":"Thermal pools reached through a lit volcanic cave tunnel, ~20 min out","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Temazcal ceremony","si_tag":"Wellness","status":"future","hook":"Pre-Hispanic sweat-lodge ritual — authentic wellness with cultural depth","bookable_category":"guided ceremony (hotel or specialist)","tier":"premier","commission_path":"activity affiliate / hotel spa","source":"https://mexicotravel.blog/la-gruta-spa-hot-springs-san-miguel-de-allende/ (Accessed 2026-07-05)","timing":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wellness","blurb":"Pre-Hispanic sweat-lodge ritual — authentic wellness with cultural depth","when":"Wedding waves Oct–Nov and Mar–May","commission":"activity affiliate / hotel spa","accessed":"2026-07-05"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is San Miguel de Allende safe to visit — it''s a Level 3 state?","a":"Bookable with a mandatory Level 3 disclosure. Guanajuato is a **Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\"** state with no named carve-out, so we disclose that plainly — but the risk is the **Highway 45D corridor to the south (Celaya, Salamanca, Irapuato)**, not the SMA historic center, which is widely reported among the safest in Mexico. Stay in the tourist zone and use vetted transfers from BJX or Querétaro.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The southern industrial corridor, plus altitude and cobblestones. The Level 3 driver is oil-theft (\"huachicol\") violence south along Hwy 45D — do not self-drive those routes. In town, the practical notes are a high-desert **~1,900 m** altitude (mild first-day effects) and steep cobblestone streets; Hospital MAC handles ER/ICU care, with advanced-trauma evac to Querétaro (~1 hr).","source":"travel.state.gov / hospitalesmac.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is SMA good for a destination wedding, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"Yes — it''s Mexico''s wedding capital, with a decades-deep planner/vendor ecosystem and venues for **20–300 guests**. The lead time is long: serious venue/planner inquiry runs **6–12 months** before the date, with the **Oct–Nov and Mar–May** weekends going first, so fire villa blocks a full engagement season ahead.","source":"destinationweddings.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What are the must-see culture sites?","a":"The pink Parroquia de San Miguel Arcángel over the Jardín, the UNESCO historic center, the Fábrica La Aurora art complex, and — ~15 min north — the Santuario de Atotonilco (1740–1776), the \"Sistine Chapel of the Americas,\" with six chapels of floor-to-ceiling baroque murals.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What''s the wellness scene?","a":"Thermal and ceremonial. La Gruta''s hot springs run **37–40 °C**, reached through a ~20 m lit volcanic cave tunnel, and temazcal (pre-Hispanic sweat-lodge) ceremonies pair with hotel-spa culture like Belmond''s Laja Spa — honeymoon-ready restoration.","source":"mexicotravel.blog, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"Is there a wine route?","a":"Yes — the under-the-radar Guanajuato wine route an hour from town, anchored by Cuna de Tierra (the state''s oldest winery) and Viñedos San Miguel, and paired with Dolores Hidalgo''s independence history and famous *nieves exóticas* (exotic ice creams).","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culinary"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Miguel de Allende Travel & Wedding Guide — World''s Best Small City | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"The world''s ''Best Small City'' and Mexico''s destination-wedding capital: the pink Parroquia, hacienda + villa weddings, hot-air balloons over the Bajío, Atotonilco, Dolores Hidalgo, the Guanajuato wine route. Bookable with mandatory L3 disclosure.","slug":"san-miguel-de-allende-mexico","primary_keyword":"San Miguel de Allende travel guide","long_tail":["San Miguel de Allende wedding venues 2026","is San Miguel de Allende safe 2026","best luxury hotels San Miguel de Allende","hot air balloon San Miguel de Allende","Atotonilco Sistine Chapel of the Americas","Dolores Hidalgo day trip","Guanajuato wine route","things to do San Miguel de Allende"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["boda San Miguel de Allende","¿es seguro viajar a San Miguel de Allende?","hoteles de lujo San Miguel de Allende","vuelo en globo San Miguel de Allende","Santuario de Atotonilco","ruta del vino Guanajuato","qué hacer en San Miguel de Allende","nieves exóticas Dolores Hidalgo"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-05"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"},{"si":"wellness","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Rosewood San Miguel de Allende","why_ultra":"Hacienda-style flagship in a transformed 16th-c colonial building; Luna rooftop with Parroquia views; spa; top wedding property","earning":"on application / Rosewood Elite via Virtuoso/Fora","mor":true,"tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa de Sierra Nevada, A Belmond Hotel","why_ultra":"37 rooms across six 17th–18th-c colonial buildings; Laja Spa; UNESCO-center heritage-luxury icon + premier wedding host","earning":"on application / Belmond Bellini Club via Virtuoso/Fora","mor":true,"tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Live Aqua San Miguel de Allende","why_ultra":"Sensory-luxury adults-oriented boutique; serene design + spa; luxury-wedding/honeymoon fit","earning":"on application / host program","mor":true,"tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Hotel Matilda (Design Hotels)","why_ultra":"Contemporary Mexican design-luxury, serious art collection, glamour crowd","earning":"on application / Design Hotels / Fora lane","mor":true,"tier":"luxury-boutique"},{"name":"Numu (Marriott Autograph Collection)","why_ultra":"44 rooms/suites, rooftop pool with colonial-skyline views, modern-heritage design","earning":"Marriott STARS/Luminous via host","mor":true,"tier":"premier-luxury"},{"name":"L''Ôtel","why_ultra":"Intimate design boutique in the historic center; couples/honeymoon fit","earning":"on application / host program","mor":true,"tier":"premier-luxury"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-05","hero":{"query":"San Miguel de Allende, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.9153,"lng":-100.7436}}'::jsonb, 101),
  ('san-sebastian-del-oeste-mexico', '10S', 'San Sebastián del Oeste', 'Mexico', '*If it''s a fog-wrapped colonial mining town in the', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Jalisco (Puerto Vallarta & Guadalajara)', '{"culture","expedition","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Colonial Sierra Madre Pueblo Mágico ~65 km / 1.5–2 hr NE of Puerto Vallarta via Hwy 544 (Source: mexicotravelsecrets.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Settled 1605; gold-mining town into the early 20th c.; mining museum + Mina Santa Gertrudis mine cave (Source: mexicotravelsecrets.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","~1,480 m elevation — cool (~25°C) when the coast is hot/humid (Source: mexicotravelsecrets.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Organic café de altura (La Quinta Mary, Hacienda Jalisco grows/roasts its own) (Source: savoteur.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Cerro de la Bufa viewpoint over Banderas Bay; Mexico''s #2 raicilla producer (Source: forbes.com.mx, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Small paved airstrip with light-aircraft (Cessna) day service from Puerto Vallarta (Source: puertovallarta.net, Accessed 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"No trauma hospital in the mountains; nearest full ER/trauma is Puerto Vallarta (AMERIMED trauma ER, CMQ Premiere, Hospiten) ~1.5–2 hr back down winding Sierra road; air-evac to US for critical cases","advisory_level":"L3","book_enabled":false,"tourist_zone_carveout":"none (Sierra Pueblo Mágico, NOT a named carve-out)","air_access_verified":"via PVR ~1.5–2 hr mountain ground (not into a carve-out); small airstrip with light-aircraft day service exists — verify current schedule","malaria":"none","dengue":"lower at ~1,480 m altitude than coast; not zero — precautions in wet months","yellow_fever":"not required"},"timing":{"peak":"November–May (dry season, coffee harvest, clear La Bufa bay views; PV high season feeds day-trips)","shoulder":"June & October","green":"July–September (wet season, foggier/rainier mountain roads, ~1,000–1,400 mm annual)","booking_lead":"Days for a PV day-tour; 2–4+ weeks for tiny boutique hacienda rooms on winter weekends","off_season_specials":"Green-season lush Sierra + coffee-country escape from coastal heat; disclose rain + mountain-road risk","event_peaks":"PV high season (Dec–Apr), Semana Santa, coffee-harvest window (local festival dates verify)","campaign_start":"Early fall into PV winter arrivals; summer ''cool-mountain escape'' value to PV visitors"},"jewels":[{"name":"Colonial center + mining museums","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Near-intact 18th-c. plaza/church + mining museum + Mina Santa Gertrudis","bookable_category":"day-tour stop / free stroll","tier":"essential","commission_path":"PV day-tour or curated-recommend","source":"https://www.mexicotravelsecrets.com/san-sebastian-del-oeste-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Near-intact 18th-c. plaza/church + mining museum + Mina Santa Gertrudis","when":"year-round","commission":"PV day-tour or curated-recommend","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"La Quinta Mary coffee-plantation tour","si_tag":"Culinary / Coffee","status":"future","hook":"Organic café de altura, artisanal-process tour","bookable_category":"plantation tour","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day-tour add-on","source":"https://savoteur.com/san-sebastian-del-oeste-jalisco-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Culinary / Coffee","blurb":"Organic café de altura, artisanal-process tour","when":"November–May","commission":"day-tour add-on","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Raicilla tasting","si_tag":"Culinary / Coffee","status":"future","hook":"Mexico''s #2 raicilla producer; agave-lechuguilla craft spirit","bookable_category":"tasting stop","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day-tour add-on / curated","source":"https://forbes.com.mx/forbes-life/viajes-pueblo-magico-de-san-sebastia-del-oeste-en-jalisco/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Culinary / Coffee","blurb":"Mexico''s #2 raicilla producer; agave-lechuguilla craft spirit","when":"November–May","commission":"day-tour add-on / curated","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Hacienda Jalisco visit","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"19th-c. hacienda that stored precious metals for Spain; grows/roasts its own coffee","bookable_category":"day-tour / boutique overnight","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"curated-recommend (direct-only lodging)","source":"https://www.banderasnews.com/travel-outdoors/hacienda-jalisco.htm (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"19th-c. hacienda that stored precious metals for Spain; grows/roasts its own coffee","when":"November–May","commission":"curated-recommend (direct-only lodging)","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Cerro de la Bufa viewpoint + summit trail","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"Short hikes to a Banderas Bay panorama + sunrise vantage","bookable_category":"guided hike / self-walk","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day-tour / guide","source":"https://forbes.com.mx/forbes-life/viajes-pueblo-magico-de-san-sebastia-del-oeste-en-jalisco/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","blurb":"Short hikes to a Banderas Bay panorama + sunrise vantage","when":"year-round","commission":"day-tour / guide","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Sierra Madre forest hikes + rappelling","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"Cool-mountain pine-oak forest walks + adventure","bookable_category":"licensed guide/operator","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate / day-tour","source":"https://www.mexicotravelsecrets.com/san-sebastian-del-oeste-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Cool-mountain pine-oak forest walks + adventure","when":"November–May","commission":"activity affiliate / day-tour","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can I book a stay in San Sebastián del Oeste?","a":"No — it is content-only, recommended only as a licensed day-trip from the Puerto Vallarta carve-out. Jalisco is US State Dept Level 3 (May 29, 2026), San Sebastián is not one of the four named carve-outs, and the advisory does not mention the town at all — so book_enabled=FALSE.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The mountain road transfer, not the town. The ~65 km / 1.5–2 hr drive on Hwy 544 leaves the PV safe zone through non-carve-out Sierra — the hold reason — and fog on narrow roads makes daytime, licensed transport essential. The nearest trauma hospital is ~1.5–2 hr back down in Puerto Vallarta.","source":"travel.state.gov / puertovallarta.net, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is there to see in the colonial town?","a":"A 17th-century time capsule. Settled in 1605 for gold, San Sebastián keeps a near-intact 18th-century plaza and church, a mining museum, and the Mina Santa Gertrudis (~60 m mine cave); it is quiet and cool at ~1,480 m. Clearest touring is November–May.","source":"mexicotravelsecrets.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What''s the coffee-and-raicilla scene like?","a":"It is the town''s signature taste. The Sierra grows organic *café de altura* — La Quinta Mary is a 19th-century estate offering artisanal-process tours, and Hacienda Jalisco grows, processes and roasts its own — and San Sebastián is Mexico''s #2 raicilla producer, a craft spirit distinct from tequila.","source":"savoteur.com / forbes.com.mx, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the hiking like at Cerro de la Bufa?","a":"Short but remote. Cerro de la Bufa offers a viewpoint and summit trail with a panorama over Banderas Bay — the coast you left, seen from ~1,480 m and higher; go guided, start early on a clear dry-season morning, and turn back in fog, since trauma care is 1.5–2 hr away in PV.","source":"forbes.com.mx, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Sebastián del Oeste Travel Guide — Jalisco''s Colonial Coffee-Mountain Pueblo Mágico | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Jalisco''s fog-wrapped 1605 mining town in the Sierra Madre — café de altura, raicilla, Cerro de la Bufa bay views, and accurate guidance: a Level-3-interior day-trip from Puerto Vallarta, not a bookable base.","slug":"san-sebastian-del-oeste-mexico","primary_keyword":"San Sebastián del Oeste Mexico travel guide","long_tail":["day trip San Sebastián del Oeste from Puerto Vallarta","San Sebastián del Oeste coffee tour","is San Sebastián del Oeste safe","Cerro de la Bufa hike","Hacienda Jalisco San Sebastián"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San Sebastián del Oeste","San Sebastián del Oeste desde Puerto Vallarta tour de un día","café de altura San Sebastián del Oeste","raicilla San Sebastián del Oeste","Cerro de la Bufa mirador","Hacienda Jalisco San Sebastián del Oeste"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"expedition","status":"future"},{"si":"Culinary / Coffee","status":"future"}],"ultra":[],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"San Sebastián del Oeste, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.7667,"lng":-104.8433}}'::jsonb, 102),
  ('santiago-chile', '10S', 'Santiago, Chile', 'Chile', 'Andean city under a 300-metre deck **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Santiago & Central Valley Wine', '{"romance","expedition","culinary","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"131","emergency_all":{"ambulance_samu":"131","police_carabineros":"133","fire_bomberos":"132"},"advisory_level":"L2","advisory_source":"travel.state.gov, updated 2026-05-20, accessed 2026-07-07","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"why_l2":"urban crime + periodic civil unrest concentrated in central Santiago (muggings, pickpocketing, distraction/phone theft, protest cycles); Araucania/Arauco/Biobio state-of-emergency is far south, not Santiago","urban_crime_caution":"street-smart in Centro/Bellavista at night; distraction/phone/bag snatch in crowds/metro/markets; vetted taxi/ride-hail over street hails; avoid demonstrations","water":"potable (hard, chlorinated; sensitive stomachs may prefer bottled)","smog_note":"winter (Apr-Aug) thermal-inversion smog in the city bowl — respiratory-sensitive caveat, not a stopper","altitude_note":"Embalse el Yeso ~2,500 m and Valle Nevado 3,000 m — mild-AMS caveat on day-trips","evac_chain":"Santiago is Chile''s top medical center (Clínica Las Condes / Alemana / Santa María) -> US-directed air-evac via insurance for catastrophic cases; travel/medical insurance still indicated"},"timing":{"peak":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr (vendimia); summer Dec-Feb hot/quieter city","winter":"Jun-Aug Andes ski (Portillo 2026 Jun 20 -> Sep 26; Valle Nevado; deepest snow Aug-early Sep) — also city smog season","shoulder":["Sep-Nov","Mar-Apr"],"booking_window":"iconic winery tours + ski-week lodging weeks-to-months ahead in high season; city hotels flexible","inflection":"vendimia curve starts mid-summer; ski curve starts at resort open-date announcements; spring curve starts late winter","fire_date":"late-Jan/early-Feb for vendimia (Mar-Apr); late-Apr/early-May for ski (Jun-Sep); mid/late-Jul for spring (curve-start minus 1-2 weeks)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Maipo Valley icon wineries — Concha y Toro (Pirque) + Almaviva","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","commission_path":"guided Maipo wine-day (DMC lane)","source":"https://www.winerist.com/country/chile/wine-region/maipo-valley","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Chile''s most storied Cabernet appellation, 30–60 min from the city: Concha y Toro''s antique gardens and the Casillero del Diablo cellar","si":"culinary","blurb":"Chile''s most storied Cabernet appellation, 30–60 min from the city: Concha y Toro''s antique gardens and the Casillero del Diablo cellar","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"guided Maipo wine-day (DMC lane)"},{"name":"Central-Valley wine day (Santa Rita + Undurraga + Cousiño Macul)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","commission_path":"full-day wine-tour package","source":"https://maipovalleywinetours.com/en/","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the classic three-estate full-day loop through the valley an hour from Santiago; historic cellars, gardens, lunch","si":"culinary","blurb":"the classic three-estate full-day loop through the valley an hour from Santiago; historic cellars, gardens, lunch","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"full-day wine-tour package"},{"name":"Mercado Central seafood (caldillo de congrio)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","commission_path":"food-tour add-on / direct table","source":"https://blog.travelhackfun.com/en/santiago-chile/","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Santiago''s historic iron-framed fish market: the place for caldillo de congrio and fresh Pacific seafood in a buzzing hall","si":"culinary","blurb":"Santiago''s historic iron-framed fish market: the place for caldillo de congrio and fresh Pacific seafood in a buzzing hall","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"food-tour add-on / direct table"},{"name":"Lastarria / Bellas Artes dining","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","commission_path":"food-and-wine walking tour / direct dining","source":"https://worldlyadventurer.com/things-to-do-in-santiago-chile/","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"cobblestone gastronomy district: contemporary Chilean tables, wine bars, the GAM and MAVI art institutions steps away","si":"culinary","blurb":"cobblestone gastronomy district: contemporary Chilean tables, wine bars, the GAM and MAVI art institutions steps away","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"food-and-wine walking tour / direct dining"},{"name":"Pomaire — pottery + pastel de choclo","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"half/full-day cultural + culinary tour","source":"https://www.visitchile.com/en/blog/pomaire--where-it-is-18-all-year-round/","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the pre-Columbian clay-craft village 50 km west: workshops where you can watch the wheel, 1-kg empanadas, cazuela","si":"culture","blurb":"the pre-Columbian clay-craft village 50 km west: workshops where you can watch the wheel, 1-kg empanadas, cazuela","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"half/full-day cultural + culinary tour"},{"name":"Cerro San Cristóbal + Bellavista + La Chascona (Neruda)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"heritage walking tour / funicular + museum entry","source":"https://worldlyadventurer.com/things-to-do-in-santiago-chile/","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the funicular/cable-car up to the citywide Virgin, the bohemian Bellavista barrio at its foot, and La Chascona, Pablo Neruda''s whimsical hillside house-museum","si":"culture","blurb":"the funicular/cable-car up to the citywide Virgin, the bohemian Bellavista barrio at its foot, and La Chascona, Pablo Neruda''s whimsical hillside house-museum","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"heritage walking tour / funicular + museum entry"},{"name":"Cerro Santa Lucía (1541 founding hill)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"self-guided / heritage tour","source":"https://blog.travelhackfun.com/en/santiago-chile/","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"self-guided / heritage tour"},{"name":"Sky Costanera (300 m, 360° deck)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"timed ticket (pass-through) + city-tour bundle","source":"https://www.skycostanera.cl/en","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"timed ticket (pass-through) + city-tour bundle"},{"name":"Cajón del Maipo — Embalse el Yeso + Termas de Colina","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided full-day (hotel pickup) — commissionable excursion","source":"https://www.gochile.cl/en/tours/embalse-del-yeso-and-colina-hotsprings-tour.htm","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the Andes canyon day: a turquoise 2,500 m reservoir ringed by snow peaks, and nine volcano-fed open-air hot-spring pools","si":"expedition","blurb":"the Andes canyon day: a turquoise 2,500 m reservoir ringed by snow peaks, and nine volcano-fed open-air hot-spring pools","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"guided full-day (hotel pickup) — commissionable excursion"},{"name":"Valle Nevado ski day (austral winter, 3,000 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","commission_path":"guided ski-day transfer + lift/rental","source":"https://www.ski.com/blog/comparing-chiles-iconic-ski-resorts-valle-nevado-and-portillo","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the largest resort in the Southern Hemisphere, 3,000 m and 1.5 hours from the city, part of the Tres Valles area","si":"expedition","blurb":"the largest resort in the Southern Hemisphere, 3,000 m and 1.5 hours from the city, part of the Tres Valles area","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"guided ski-day transfer + lift/rental"},{"name":"Portillo (Ski Portillo, ~2 hrs — Jun 20–Sep 26 2026)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"guided ski-week / transfer package","source":"https://www.ski.com/blog/when-to-ski-in-chile-and-argentina","timing":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Spring Sep-Nov + autumn harvest Mar-Apr","commission":"guided ski-week / transfer package"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can you do a wine tour from Santiago?","a":"Yes — the Maipo Valley, Chile''s oldest and most decorated Cabernet appellation, is a 30-to-60-minute drive from the city, with icons like Concha y Toro (Pirque) and Almaviva (the 1997 Rothschild × Concha y Toro joint venture). Iconic winery tours book weeks-to-months ahead in high season, so reserve early.","source":"winerist.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What are the top things to do in Santiago?","a":"Start high: Sky Costanera''s 360° deck sits at 300 m on floors 61–62 of South America''s tallest building, and Cerro San Cristóbal rises ~880 m inside the 722-hectare Parque Metropolitano to a 14-m Virgin visible citywide. Add Neruda''s La Chascona, Lastarria dining, and the Mercado Central seafood halls.","source":"skycostanera.cl, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Santiago a good base for a romantic or luxe stay?","a":"Yes — the city carries a real luxe hotel bench with built-in romance. The Singular (Leading Hotels of the World), the Mandarin Oriental (the group''s first South American property), and the 196-room W anchor Andes-view rooftops and wine-estate lunches; Viña Vik''s 22 designer suites sit about two hours south.","source":"virtuoso.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you ski from Santiago?","a":"Yes, in austral winter. Valle Nevado — the largest ski resort in the Southern Hemisphere at 3,000 m — is about 60 km / 1.5 hours from the city, a true day-trip from a hotel. Iconic Portillo, two hours out, runs its 2026 season June 20 → September 26.","source":"ski.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Santiago safe for tourists right now?","a":"Yes — it is freely bookable at Level 2 (last updated May 20, 2026). The level reflects urban crime and periodic protest concentrated in central districts; one 2025 dataset attributed about 78% of tourist-related incidents to Santiago Centro, Las Condes, and Providencia. The southern Araucanía state-of-emergency is far away and untouched by this itinerary.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-20","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real day-to-day risk in Santiago?","a":"Theft, not wilderness. The everyday risk is muggings, pickpocketing, and distraction/phone-snatch theft in crowded plazas, the metro, and markets, plus occasional protest cycles that can disrupt transit. Keep phones away in crowds, use vetted taxis or ride-hailing over street hails, and avoid demonstrations. Emergency numbers are 131 ambulance and 133 police.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-20","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the altitude on the ski and canyon day-trips a problem?","a":"It can be for sensitive travelers. Embalse el Yeso sits at ~2,500 m and Valle Nevado at 3,000 m, so day-trippers gain real altitude within hours of sea-level Santiago — flag mild-AMS risk, hydrate, and acclimatize. On-piste skiing is resort-operated with patrol; backcountry and off-piste avalanche terrain are guided-only.","source":"ski.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Santiago, Chile — Wine Country, the Andes, Bellavista & Sky Costanera | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-CL","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Santiago Chile","viñas Valle del Maipo","Cajón del Maipo","Embalse el Yeso tour","Concha y Toro Pirque tour","esquí Valle Nevado desde Santiago","Cerro San Cristóbal funicular","La Chascona Neruda","vendimia Valle del Maipo","restaurantes Lastarria"],"hreflang":["en","es-CL"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"The Singular Santiago","type":"Leading Hotels of the World boutique — Lastarria","earning":"luxe hotel-commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Mandarin Oriental, Santiago","type":"Andes-foot luxe — Las Condes (Virtuoso)","earning":"luxe-ultra commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"luxe-ultra"},{"name":"W Santiago","type":"196-room design hotel — Isidora Goyenechea (Virtuoso)","earning":"luxe commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Hotel Cumbres Lastarria","type":"boutique-luxe in the Lastarria district","earning":"premium-luxe commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Viña Vik","type":"Relais & Châteaux Millahue wine estate (~2 hrs south) — 22 suites, titanium-roof landmark","earning":"ultra commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"ultra"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Santiago, Chile, Chile"},"geo":{"lat":-33.4489,"lng":-70.6693}}'::jsonb, 103),
  ('sao-paulo-brazil', '10S', 'São Paulo, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'The Southern Hemisphere''s largest city **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'venice', 'Rio & The Southeast Coast', '{"romance","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","emergency_medical":"192","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/brazil-travel-advisory.html","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":{"international":"GRU (Guarulhos / São Paulo–Guarulhos International — Brazil''s largest)","domestic":"CGH (Congonhas — domestic + regional, close to city core)"},"water":"tap treated/generally potable; visitors commonly drink bottled/filtered","trauma":"Albert Einstein (#1 Latin America, top-30 world) + Sírio-Libanês (#2 Latin America) for stabilization; US medical evacuation for serious cases","caveats":["Favelas / informal housing developments = L4 Do Not Travel, even on guided tours","Crime + kidnapping risk indicators (Brazil-wide)","District-driven urban crime: safe core = Jardins/Itaim Bibi/Paulista/Pinheiros/Vila Madalena","Centro (old downtown) = daytime-only mission; leave before dark","Cracolândia (Luz / Campos Elíseos) = avoid entirely, day or night","Phone-snatching / anti-snatch discipline in crowds","Date-drug / drink-spiking robberies (Brazil advisory)","Vetted transport only after dark (Uber / registered taxi; not municipal buses at night)","Dengue precautions (repellent)"]},"timing":{"peak":"Year-round (business + trade fairs — WTM Latin America mid-April; MICE all cycle)","inflection":"~3–4 weeks before each event spike (F1: mid-October; Carnaval: mid-January)","fire_date":"curve-start − 1–2 weeks → late September / early October for the F1 spike; early January for Carnaval; culinary-weekend layer fires any month (attach to curve as gateway/stopover)","shoulder":"Rolling culinary-weekend + design-hotel layer, any month","low":"Jun–Aug (austral winter — cooler, drier, comfortable for a food-and-art city); off-season fill with culinary + museum + design-hotel weekends","event_peaks":[{"event":"Formula 1 São Paulo Grand Prix (Interlagos)","dates":"2026-11-06 to 2026-11-08","note":"hotels tighten across race week; travelers stay in city core (~25km from circuit)"},{"event":"Carnaval 2026 (street blocos + Sambódromo do Anhembi)","dates":"2026-02-13 to 2026-02-17","note":"630 blocos programmed; SP does not surcharge as hard as Rio, Sambódromo ~40–60% cheaper — value-Carnaval angle"}]},"jewels":[{"name":"A Casa do Porco","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC culinary program carries margin; table booked direct / non-commissionable","source":"https://www.theworlds50best.com/latinamerica/en/the-list/a-casa-do-porco.html","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Jefferson Rueda''s pork-gospel tasting house, arguably Brazil''s most famous restaurant; a ~US$40 tasting menu, no dress code, ranked 25 in Latin America''s 50 Best","si":"culinary","blurb":"Jefferson Rueda''s pork-gospel tasting house, arguably Brazil''s most famous restaurant; a ~US$40 tasting menu, no dress code, ranked 25 in Latin America''s 50 Best","when":"Year-round","commission":"DMC culinary program carries margin; table booked direct / non-commissionable"},{"name":"D.O.M. (Alex Atala, 2 Michelin stars)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"ultra","commission_path":"DMC culinary program for margin; table direct","source":"https://guide.michelin.com/en/article/dining-out/all-michelin-starred-restaurants-in-sao-paulo","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Year-round","commission":"DMC culinary program for margin; table direct"},{"name":"Evvai & Tuju (first Latin American 3 Michelin stars)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"ultra","commission_path":"DMC / concierge access for margin; table direct","source":"https://guide.michelin.com/en/article/dining-out/all-michelin-starred-restaurants-in-sao-paulo","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Year-round","commission":"DMC / concierge access for margin; table direct"},{"name":"Maní (Helena Rizzo, 1 Michelin star)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC culinary program for margin; table direct","source":"https://guide.michelin.com/en/article/dining-out/all-michelin-starred-restaurants-in-sao-paulo","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Year-round","commission":"DMC culinary program for margin; table direct"},{"name":"Mercadão — Municipal Market + mortadella sandwich","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","commission_path":"food-tour affiliate (GetYourGuide/Viator); entry free","source":"https://streetsmartbrazil.com/sao-paulos-mercadao-municipal-market-meeting-place/","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the eclectic 1933 market hall under stained glass; the fist-sized mortadella sandwich is the pilgrimage bite, plus pastel de bacalhau and tropical-fruit stalls","si":"culinary","blurb":"the eclectic 1933 market hall under stained glass; the fist-sized mortadella sandwich is the pilgrimage bite, plus pastel de bacalhau and tropical-fruit stalls","when":"Year-round","commission":"food-tour affiliate (GetYourGuide/Viator); entry free"},{"name":"Liberdade — Japanese quarter + weekend fair","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","commission_path":"food/culture-tour affiliate; self-guided free","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g303631-d2350042-Reviews-Liberdade_Street_Market-Sao_Paulo_State_of_Sao_Paulo.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the largest Japanese community outside Japan; torii gate, red lanterns, weekend arts-and-food fair, sushi counters and Okinawan bakeries. A culinary + cultural double-header","si":"culinary","blurb":"the largest Japanese community outside Japan; torii gate, red lanterns, weekend arts-and-food fair, sushi counters and Okinawan bakeries. A culinary + cultural double-header","when":"year-round","commission":"food/culture-tour affiliate; self-guided free"},{"name":"MASP + Avenida Paulista (Sunday car-free)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"culture-tour affiliate; MASP entry non-commissionable","source":"https://www.kupi.com/en/explore/brazil/sao-paulo/sao-paulo-museum-of-art","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Lina Bo Bardi''s icon floating on red pillars over the avenue, holding Rembrandt, Van Gogh, Renoir, Picasso and a deep Brazilian collection","si":"culture","blurb":"Lina Bo Bardi''s icon floating on red pillars over the avenue, holding Rembrandt, Van Gogh, Renoir, Picasso and a deep Brazilian collection","when":"Year-round","commission":"culture-tour affiliate; MASP entry non-commissionable"},{"name":"Pinacoteca + Farol Santander view","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"culture-tour affiliate; entries non-commissionable","source":"https://www.nomadicmatt.com/travel-guides/brazil-travel-tips/sao-paulo/","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the city''s oldest art museum, the great collection of Brazilian works, paired with the Farol Santander observation deck for the skyline","si":"culture","blurb":"the city''s oldest art museum, the great collection of Brazilian works, paired with the Farol Santander observation deck for the skyline","when":"Year-round","commission":"culture-tour affiliate; entries non-commissionable"},{"name":"Ibirapuera Park + Oscar Niemeyer (Oca / MAC / Afro-Brasil)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"culture-tour affiliate / self-guided; museum entries non-commissionable","source":"https://www.nomadicmatt.com/travel-guides/brazil-travel-tips/sao-paulo/","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"South America''s great urban park, the Niemeyer-designed Oca, Auditório and MAC/Afro-Brasil museums; footvolley, bike paths, and modernist architecture in one green sweep","si":"culture","blurb":"South America''s great urban park, the Niemeyer-designed Oca, Auditório and MAC/Afro-Brasil museums; footvolley, bike paths, and modernist architecture in one green sweep","when":"Year-round","commission":"culture-tour affiliate / self-guided; museum entries non-commissionable"},{"name":"Beco do Batman street art (Vila Madalena)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"street-art walking-tour affiliate; self-guided free (daytime)","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g303631-d2349935-Reviews-Batman_Alley-Sao_Paulo_State_of_Sao_Paulo.html","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Crowds, phone-snatching around the alley, night caution Daytime unguided fine; guided street-art tour adds context; keep the phone secured","si":"culture","blurb":"Crowds, phone-snatching around the alley, night caution Daytime unguided fine; guided street-art tour adds context; keep the phone secured","when":"Year-round","commission":"street-art walking-tour affiliate; self-guided free (daytime)"},{"name":"Vila Madalena bar night","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","commission_path":"nightlife / bar-crawl tour affiliate; DMC private evening","source":"https://www.leftturnstravel.com/post/neighborhood-guide-to-vila-madalena","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the bohemian nightlife epicenter: Astor, Pé de Manga, Bar do Baixo, Pracinha do Seu Justino","si":"romance","blurb":"the bohemian nightlife epicenter: Astor, Pé de Manga, Bar do Baixo, Pracinha do Seu Justino","when":"Year-round","commission":"nightlife / bar-crawl tour affiliate; DMC private evening"},{"name":"Helicopter skyline tour (Campo de Marte)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","commission_path":"helicopter-tour affiliate (GetYourGuide/Viator) / DMC","source":"https://passeiodehelicoptero.com/en/helicopter-tour-sao-paulo/","timing":"Year-round","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Operator air-safety, weather windows, boarding logistics Guided only — licensed, insured operator; confirm the flight departs Campo de Marte and includes transfer","si":"romance","blurb":"Operator air-safety, weather windows, boarding logistics Guided only — licensed, insured operator; confirm the flight departs Campo de Marte and includes transfer","when":"Year-round","commission":"helicopter-tour affiliate (GetYourGuide/Viator) / DMC"}],"faq":null,"seo":{"meta_title":"São Paulo Travel Guide 2026 — Latin America''s Food Capital, MASP, Ibirapuera & Design Hotels | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"pt-BR","local_keywords":["o que fazer em São Paulo","melhores restaurantes SP","MASP Avenida Paulista","Ibirapuera o que fazer","Beco do Batman Vila Madalena","Mercadão sanduíche de mortadela","bairro da Liberdade São Paulo","São Paulo é seguro para turistas","onde ficar em São Paulo Jardins Itaim","melhores hotéis de luxo em São Paulo","passeio de helicóptero São Paulo"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Rosewood São Paulo (Cidade Matarazzo)","lane":"Virtuoso/Fora","mor":"consortia","tier":"ultra","note":"Jean Nouvel + Philippe Starck; the flagship opening"},{"name":"Pa